<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="EXO" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Exodus</para>
  <para style="mt">Exodus</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> the names of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which came into Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; every man and his household came with Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son] [Behold a Son]</char>, Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char>, Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>, and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>, Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>, and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, and Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>, Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char>, and Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And all the souls that came out of the waist of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> were seventy souls: for Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char> was in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place] [already]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char> died, and all his brethren, and all that generation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were fruitful, and increased abundantly, and multiplied, and waxed exceeding mighty; and the land was filled with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now there arose up a new king over Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, which knew not Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he said unto his people, Behold, the people of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [are]</char> more and mightier than we:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Come on, let us deal wisely with them; lest they multiply, and it come to pass, that, when there falls out any war, they join also unto our enemies, and fight against us, and <char style="add">[so]</char> get them up out of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Therefore they did set over them taskmasters to afflict them with their burdens. And they built for Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> treasure cities, Pitom <char style="add">[City of Justice]</char> and Ra’amses <char style="add">[Child of the Sun]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But the more they afflicted them, the more they multiplied and grew. And they were grieved because of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the Mitzri made the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to serve with rigour:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they made their lives bitter with hard bondage, in mortar, and in brick, and in all manner of service in the field: all their service, wherein they made them serve, <char style="add">[was]</char> with rigour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> spoke to the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> midwives, of which the name of the one <char style="add">[was]</char> Shif’rah <char style="add">[Beautiful]</char>, and the name of the other Puah <char style="add">[Splendid]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he said, When you<char style="ord">2f</char> do the office of a midwife to the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> women, and see <char style="add">[them]</char> upon the stools; if it <char style="add">[be]</char> a son, then you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall kill him: but if it <char style="add">[be]</char> a daughter, then she shall live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But the midwives feared God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and did not as the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> commanded them, but saved the men children alive.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> called for the midwives, and said unto them, Why have you<char style="ord">2f</char> done this thing, and have saved the men children alive?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the midwives said unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, Because the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> women <char style="add">[are]</char> not as the Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char> women; for they <char style="add">[are]</char> lively, and are delivered before the midwives come in unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Therefore God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> dealt well with the midwives: and the people multiplied, and waxed very mighty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And it came to pass, because the midwives feared God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that he made them houses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> charged all his people, saying, Khav’vah <char style="add">[Eve]</char> <char style="pn">(to breath, to live)</char> every son that is born you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall cast into the river, and every daughter you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall save alive.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And there went a man of the house of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>, and took <char style="add">[to wife]</char> a daughter of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the woman conceived, and bore a son: and when she saw him that he <char style="add">[was a]</char> goodly <char style="add">[child]</char>, she hid him three months.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when she could no longer hide him, she took for him an ark of bulrushes, and daubed it with slime and with pitch, and put the child in it; and she laid <char style="add">[it]</char> in the flags by the river’s brink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And his sister stood afar off, that is to say what would be done to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the daughter of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> came down to wash <char style="add">[herself]</char> at the river; and her maidens walked along by the river’s side; and when she saw the ark among the flags, she sent her maid to fetch it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when she had opened <char style="add">[it]</char>, she saw the child: and, behold, the babe wept. And she had compassion on him, and said, This <char style="add">[is one]</char> of the ‘Evrim <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> children.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then said his sister to Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> daughter, Shall I go and call to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> a nurse of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> women, that she may nurse the child for you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> daughter said to her, Go. And the maid went and called the child’s mother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> daughter said unto her, Take this child away, and nurse it for me, and I will give <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> wages. And the woman took the child, and nursed it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the child grew, and she brought him unto Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> daughter, and he became her son. And she called his name Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>: and she said, Because I drew him out of the water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass in those days, when Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> was grown, that he went out unto his brethren, and looked on their burdens: and he spied an Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char> attacking an ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char>, one of his brethren.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he looked this way and that way, and when he saw that <char style="add">[there was]</char> no man, he killed the Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char>, and hid him in the sand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And when he went out the second day, behold, two men of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> strove together: and he said to him that did the wrong, For what reason strike you<char style="ord">i</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> fellow?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said, Who made you<char style="ord">i</char> a prince and a judge over us? intend you<char style="ord">i</char> to kill me, as you<char style="ord">i</char> killed the Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char>? And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> feared, and said, Surely this thing is known.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now when Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heard this thing, he sought to slay Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>. But Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> fled from the face of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and dwelt in the land of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>: and he sat down by a well.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Now the priest of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char> had seven daughters: and they came and drew <char style="add">[water]</char>, and filled the troughs to water their father’s flock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the shepherds came and drove them away: but Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> stood up and helped them, and watered their flock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when they came to Reu’el <char style="add">[Friend of God]</char> their father, he said, How <char style="add">[is it that]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> are come so soon to day?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they said, An Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char> delivered us out of the hand of the shepherds, and also drew <char style="add">[water]</char> enough for us, and watered the flock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he said unto his daughters, And where <char style="add">[is]</char> he? why <char style="add">[is]</char> it <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> have left the man? call him, that he may eat bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> was content to dwell with the man: and he gave Moshe his daughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And she bore <char style="add">[him]</char> a son, and he called his name Gershom <char style="add">[Exiled One]</char>: for he said, I have been a stranger in a strange land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it came to pass in process of time, that the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> died: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sighed by reason of the bondage, and they cried, and their cry came up unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> by reason of the bondage.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> heard their groaning, and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> remembered his covenant with Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, with Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and with Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> looked upon the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Creator]</char> had respect unto <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> kept the flock of Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char> his father in law, the priest of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>: and he led the flock to the backside of the desert, and came to the mountain of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> to Horev <char style="add">[Desert]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush <char style="add">[was]</char> not consumed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, I will now turn aside, and see this great sight, why the bush is not burnt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> saw that he turned aside to see, God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Living Word]</char> called unto him out of the midst of the bush, and said, Moshe, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>. And he said, Here <char style="add">[am]</char> I.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he said, Draw not near here: put off you<char style="ord">i</char> shoes from off you<char style="ord">i</char> feet, for the place whereon you<char style="ord">i</char> stand <char style="add">[is]</char> holy ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Moreover he said, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of your<char style="ord">i</char> father, the God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Powerful Living Word]</char> of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Powerful One]</char> of Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and the God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Powerful Creator]</char> of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>. And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> hid his face; for he was afraid to look upon God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Living Word]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, I have surely seen the affliction of my people which <char style="add">[are]</char> in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and have heard their cry by reason of their taskmasters; for I know their sorrows;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I am come down to deliver them out of the hand of the Mitzri, and to bring them up out of that land unto a good land and a large, unto a land flowing with milk and honey; unto the place of the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, and the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>, and the Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Now therefore, behold, the cry of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is come unto me: and I have also seen the oppression which the Mitzri oppress them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Come now therefore, and I will send you<char style="ord">i</char> unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may bring forth my people the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, Who <char style="add">[am]</char> I, that I should go unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and that I should bring forth the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of Mitzrayim [Egypt - The Narrow Place]?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he said, Certainly, I will be with you<char style="ord">i</char>; and this <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a token unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, that I have sent you<char style="ord">i</char>: When you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought forth the people out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall serve God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> upon this mountain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, Behold, <char style="add">[when]</char> I come unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and shall say unto them, The God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of your fathers has sent me unto you; and they shall say to me, What <char style="add">[is]</char> his name? what shall I say unto them?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>: Ehyeh Asher Ehyeh <char style="add">[I am/will be what I am/will be]</char> and he said, “Thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: ‘Ehyeh <char style="add">[I Am or I Will Be]</char> …has sent me unto you.”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said moreover unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: <char style="add">[The LORD-Yehōvah]</char> of your fathers, the God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[Creator]</char> of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[Creator]</char> of Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and the God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[Creator]</char> of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, has sent me unto you: this <char style="add">[is]</char> my name forever, and this <char style="add">[is]</char> my memorial unto all generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Go, and gather the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> together, and say unto them, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of your fathers, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, of Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, appeared unto me, saying, I have surely visited you, and <char style="add">[seen]</char> that which is done to you in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And I have said, I will bring you up out of the affliction of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> unto the land of the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, and the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>, and the Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, unto a land flowing with milk and honey.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And they shall hearken to you<char style="ord">i</char> voice: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come, you<char style="ord">i</char> and the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, unto the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall say unto him, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Living Word]</char> of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrews]</char> has met with us: and now let us go, we beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, three days’ journey into the wilderness, that we may sacrifice to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="add">[The Living Word]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And I am sure that the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> will not let you go, no, not by a mighty hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And I will stretch out my hand, and strike Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> with all my wonders which I will do in the midst thereof: and after that, he will let you go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And I will give this people favour in the sight of the Mitzri: and it shall come to pass, that, when you<char style="ord">2f</char> go, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not go empty:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But every woman shall borrow of her neighbour, and of her that sojourns in her house, jewels of silver, and jewels of gold, and clothing: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall put <char style="add">[them]</char> upon your sons, and upon your<char style="ord">2f</char> daughters; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> the Mitzri.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> answered and said, But, behold, they will not believe me, nor hearken unto my voice: for they will say, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has not appeared unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, What <char style="add">[is]</char> that in you<char style="ord">i</char> hand? And he said, A rod.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he said, Cast it on the ground. And he cast it on the ground, and it became a serpent; and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> fled from before it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Put forth you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and take it by the tail. And he put forth his hand, and caught it, and it became a rod in his hand:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />That they may believe that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, has appeared unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said furthermore unto him, Put now you<char style="ord">i</char> hand into you<char style="ord">i</char> bosom. And he put his hand into his bosom: and when he took it out, behold, his hand <char style="add">[was]</char> leprous as snow.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he said, Put you<char style="ord">i</char> hand into you<char style="ord">i</char> bosom again. And he put his hand into his bosom again; and plucked it out of his bosom, and, behold, it was turned again as his <char style="add">[other]</char> flesh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, if they will not believe you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither hearken to the voice of the first sign, that they will believe the voice of the latter sign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, if they will not believe also these two signs, neither hearken unto you<char style="ord">i</char> voice, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take of the water of the river, and pour <char style="add">[it]</char> upon the dry <char style="add">[land]</char>: and the water which you<char style="ord">i</char> take out of the river shall become blood upon the dry <char style="add">[land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, O my Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Lord Above All Things]</char>, I <char style="add">[am]</char> not eloquent, neither heretofore, nor since you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken unto you<char style="ord">i</char> servant: but I <char style="add">[am]</char> slow of speech, and of a slow tongue.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Who has made man’s mouth? or who makes the dumb, or deaf, or the seeing, or the blind? have not I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Now therefore go, and I will be with you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, and teach you<char style="ord">i</char> what you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he said, O my Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Lord Above All Things]</char>, send, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, by the hand <char style="add">[of him whom]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> will send.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was kindled against Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and he said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> not Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother? I know that he can speak well. And also, behold, he comes forth to meet you<char style="ord">i</char>: and when he sees you<char style="ord">i</char>, he will be glad in his heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak unto him, and put words in his mouth: and I will be with you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, and with his mouth, and will teach you what you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he shall be you<char style="ord">i</char> spokesman unto the people: and he shall be, <char style="add">[even]</char> he shall be to you<char style="ord">i</char> instead of a mouth, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be to him instead of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take this rod in you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do signs.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went and returned to Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char> his father in law, and said unto him, Let me go, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and return unto my brethren which <char style="add">[are]</char> in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and see whether they be yet alive. And Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char> said to Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> in Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, Go, return into Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: for all the men are dead which sought you<char style="ord">i</char> life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> took his wife and his sons, and set them upon an ass, and he returned to the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> took the rod of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, When you<char style="ord">i</char> goes to return into Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, see that you<char style="ord">i</char> do all those wonders before Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, which I have put in you<char style="ord">i</char> hand: but I will harden his heart, that he shall not let the people go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [is]</char> my son, <char style="add">[even]</char> my firstborn:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And I say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, Let my son go, that he may serve me: and if you<char style="ord">i</char> refuse to let him go, behold, I will slay you<char style="ord">i</char> son, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> firstborn.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And it came to pass by the way in the inn, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> met him, and sought to kill him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then Zipporah took a sharp stone, and cut off the foreskin of her son, and cast <char style="add">[it]</char> at his feet, and said, Surely a bloody husband <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> to me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />So he let him go: then she said, A bloody husband <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> are]</char>, because of the circumcision.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Go into the wilderness to meet Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>. And he went, and met him in the mount of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and kissed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> told Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> all the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> who had sent him, and all the signs which he had commanded him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> went and gathered together all the elders of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> spoke all the words which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had spoken unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and did the signs in the sight of the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the people believed: and when they heard that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had visited the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and that he had looked upon their affliction, then they bowed their heads and worshipped.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And afterward Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> went in, and told Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Let my people go, that they may hold a feast unto me in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> said, Who <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that I should obey his voice to let Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go? I know not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, neither will I let Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they said, The God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> has met with us: let us go, we pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, three days’ journey into the desert, and sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; lest he fall upon us with pestilence, or with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> said unto them, For what reason do you<char style="ord">2f</char>, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, let the people from their works? get you unto your burdens.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> said, Behold, the people of the land now <char style="add">[are]</char> many, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> make them rest from their burdens.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> commanded the same day the taskmasters of the people, and their officers, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall no more give the people straw to make brick, as heretofore: let them go and gather straw for themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the tale of the bricks, which they did make heretofore, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall lay upon them; you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not diminish <char style="add">[ought]</char> thereof: for they <char style="add">[be]</char> idle; therefore they cry, saying, Let us go <char style="add">[and]</char> sacrifice to our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Let there more work be laid upon the men, that they may labour in it; and let them not regard vain words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the taskmasters of the people went out, and their officers, and they spoke to the people, saying, Thus says Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, I will not give you straw.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Go you<char style="ord">2f</char>, get you straw where you<char style="ord">2f</char> can find it: yet none of your work shall be diminished.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So the people were scattered abroad throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> to gather stubble instead of straw.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the taskmasters hasted <char style="add">[them]</char>, saying, Fulfill your works, <char style="add">[your]</char> daily tasks, as when there was straw.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the officers of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> taskmasters had set over them, were beaten, <char style="add">[and]</char> demanded, For what reason have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not fulfilled your task in making brick both yesterday and today, as heretofore?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then the officers of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came and cried unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, saying, For what reason do you<char style="ord">i</char> deal thus with your<char style="ord">i</char> servants?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />There is no straw given unto you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and they say to us, Make brick: and, behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> servants <char style="add">[are]</char> beaten; but the fault <char style="add">[is]</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char> own people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But he said, You<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> idle, <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">2f</char> are]</char> idle: therefore you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, Let us go <char style="add">[and]</char> do sacrifice to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Go therefore now, <char style="add">[and]</char> work; for there shall no straw be given you, yet shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> deliver the tale of bricks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the officers of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did see <char style="add">[that]</char> they <char style="add">[were]</char> in evil <char style="add">[case]</char>, after it was said, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not diminish <char style="add">[ought]</char> from your bricks of your daily task.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And they met Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, who stood in the way, as they came forth from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they said unto them, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> look upon you, and judge; because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have made our savour to be abhorred in the eyes of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and in the eyes of his servants, to put a sword in their hand to slay us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> returned unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Lord Above All Things]</char>, wherefore have you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[so]</char> evil entreated this people? why <char style="add">[is]</char> it <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have sent me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For since I came to Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> to speak in you<char style="ord">i</char> name, he has done evil to this people; neither have you<char style="ord">i</char> delivered you<char style="ord">i</char> people at all.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Now shall you<char style="ord">i</char> see what I will do to Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>: for with a strong hand shall he let them go, and with a strong hand shall he drive them out of his land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and said unto him, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I appeared unto Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, unto Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and unto Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, by <char style="add">[the name of]</char> El-Shaddai <char style="add">[God-The Powerful Living Word]</char>, but by my name YEHOVAH was I not known to them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And I have also established my covenant with them, to give them the land of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, the land of their pilgrimage, wherein they were strangers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I have also heard the groaning of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whom the Mitzri keep in bondage; and I have remembered my covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For what reason say unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and I will bring you out from under the burdens of the Mitzri, and I will rid you out of their bondage, and I will redeem you with a stretched out arm, and with great judgments:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I will take you to me for a people, and I will be to you a God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which brings you out from under the burdens of the Mitzri.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I will bring you in unto the land, concerning the which I did swear to give it to Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, to Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and to Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>; and I will give it you for an heritage: I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> spoke so unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: but they listened not unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> for anguish of spirit, and for cruel bondage.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Go in, speak unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, that he let the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go out of his land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> spoke before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Behold, the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> have not listened unto me; how then shall Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> hear me, who <char style="add">[am]</char> of uncircumcised lips?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and gave them a charge unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, to bring the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />These <char style="add">[be]</char> the heads of their fathers’ houses: The sons of Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son]</char> the firstborn of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; Hanokh <char style="add">[Dedicated]</char>, and Pallu <char style="add">[Distinguished]</char>, Hetzron <char style="add">[surrounded by a wall]</char>, and Karmi <char style="add">[Fruitful, Noble]</char>: these <char style="add">[be]</char> the families of Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the sons of Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char>; Y’mu’el <char style="add">[Day of God]</char>, and Yamin <char style="add">[Right Hand]</char>, and Ohad <char style="add">[Praising, Confessing]</char>, and Yakhin <char style="add">[He will establish]</char>, and Tzochar <char style="add">[Shining Oil]</char>, and Sha’ul <char style="add">[Desired]</char> the son of a Kena’anit [Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchants]</char>] woman: these <char style="add">[are]</char> the families of Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> the names of the sons of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char> according to their generations; Gershon <char style="add">[Exile]</char>, and K’hat <char style="add">[assembly, congregation]</char>, and M’rari <char style="add">[Bitter]</char>: and the years of the life of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner] [were]</char> an hundred thirty and seven years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />The sons of Gershon <char style="add">[Exile]</char>; Livni <char style="add">[White]</char>, and Shimi <char style="add">[Famous]</char>, according to their families.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the sons of K’hat <char style="add">[assembly, congregation]</char>; ‘Amram <char style="add">[exalted people]</char>, and Yitz’har <char style="add">[Shining Oil]</char>, and Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, and Uzziel <char style="add">[My Strength is God]</char>: and the years of the life of K’hat <char style="add">[assembly, congregation] [were]</char> an hundred thirty and three years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the sons of M’rari <char style="add">[Bitter]</char>; Mahali <char style="add">[Infirmity]</char> and Mushi <char style="add">[Yielding]</char>: these <char style="add">[are]</char> the families of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char> according to their generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And ‘Amram <char style="add">[exalted people]</char> took him Yokheved <char style="add">[Jehovah is Glory]</char> his father’s sister to wife; and she bore him Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>: and the years of the life of ‘Amram <char style="add">[exalted people] [were]</char> an hundred and thirty and seven years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the sons of Yitz’har <char style="add">[Shining Oil]</char>; Korakh <char style="add">[Bald]</char>, and Nefeg <char style="add">[Weak, Slacked]</char>, and Zikhri <char style="add">[Illustrious]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the sons of Uzziel <char style="add">[My Strength is God]</char>; Misha’el <char style="add">[Who is what God is]</char>, and Elzafan <char style="add">[God Protects]</char>, and Sitri <char style="add">[The Lord Protects]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> took him Elisheva <char style="add">[God is Her Oath]</char>, daughter of ‘Amminadav <char style="add">[family of the prince]</char>, sister of Nachshon <char style="add">[Enchanter]</char>, to wife; and she bore him Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char>, and Avihu <char style="add">[he is my father]</char>, El’azar <char style="add">[God has helped]</char>, and Itamar <char style="add">[Coast of Palms]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the sons of Korakh <char style="add">[Bald]</char>; Asir <char style="add">[Prisoner]</char>, and Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession]</char>, and Abiasaph <char style="add">[The Father Gathers]</char>: these <char style="add">[are]</char> the families of the Korchi.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And El’azar <char style="add">[God has helped]</char> Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s son took him <char style="add">[one]</char> of the daughters of Puti’el <char style="add">[Afflicted of God]</char> to wife; and she bore him Pinchas <char style="add">[mouth of brass]</char>: these <char style="add">[are]</char> the heads of the fathers of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> according to their families.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />These <char style="add">[are]</char> that Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, to whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Bring out the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> according to their armies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />These <char style="add">[are]</char> they which spoke to Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, to bring out the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: these <char style="add">[are]</char> that Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And it came to pass on the day <char style="add">[when]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />That the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: speak you<char style="ord">i</char> unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> all that I say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> of uncircumcised lips, and how shall Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> hearken unto me?</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, See, I have made you<char style="ord">i</char> a god to Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>: and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother shall be you<char style="ord">i</char> prophet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak all that I command you<char style="ord">i</char>: and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother shall speak unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, that he send the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of his land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I will harden Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart, and multiply my signs and my wonders in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> shall not hearken unto you, that I may lay my hand upon Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and bring forth my armies, <char style="add">[and]</char> my people the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> by great judgments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the Mitzri shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I stretch forth my hand upon Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and bring out the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from among them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> did as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded them, so did they.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters] [was]</char> eighty years old, and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> eighty and three years old, when they spoke unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />When Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> shall speak unto you, saying, Show a miracle for you: then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Take you<char style="ord">i</char> rod, and cast <char style="add">[it]</char> before Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> it shall become a serpent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> went in unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and they did so as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded: and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> cast down his rod before Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and before his servants, and it became a serpent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> also called the wise men and the sorcerers: now the magicians of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, they also did in like manner with their enchantments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />For they cast down every man his rod, and they became serpents: but Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s rod swallow (to approve, commend, accept)ed up their rods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he hardened Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart, that he listened not unto them; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart <char style="add">[is]</char> hardened, he refuses to let the people go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Get you<char style="ord">i</char> unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> in the morning; lo, he goes out unto the water; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall stand by the river’s brink against he come; and the rod which was turned to a serpent shall you<char style="ord">i</char> take in you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say unto him, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> has sent me unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Let my people go, that they may serve me in the wilderness: and, behold, up to this time you<char style="ord">i</char> would not hear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, In this you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: behold, I will strike with the rod that <char style="add">[is]</char> in my hand upon the waters which <char style="add">[are]</char> in the river, and they shall be turned to blood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the fish that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the river shall die, and the river shall stink; and the Mitzri shall loathe to drink of the water of the river.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Say unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Take you<char style="ord">i</char> rod, and stretch out you<char style="ord">i</char> hand upon the waters of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, upon their streams, upon their rivers, and upon their ponds, and upon all their pools of water, that they may become blood; and <char style="add">[that]</char> there may be blood throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, both in <char style="add">[vessels of]</char> wood, and in <char style="add">[vessels of]</char> stone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> did so, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded; and he lifted up the rod, and struck the waters that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the river, in the sight of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and in the sight of his servants; and all the waters that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the river were turned to blood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the fish that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the river died; and the river stank, and the Mitzri could not drink of the water of the river; and there was blood throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the magicians of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> did so with their enchantments: and Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart was hardened, neither did he hearken unto them; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> turned and went into his house, neither did he set his heart to this also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And all the Mitzri excavated round about the river for water to drink; for they could not drink of the water of the river.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And seven days were fulfilled, after that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had smitten the river.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and say unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Let my people go, that they may serve me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And if you<char style="ord">i</char> refuse to let <char style="add">[them]</char> go, behold, I will strike all you<char style="ord">i</char> borders with frogs:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the river shall bring forth frogs abundantly, which shall go up and come into you<char style="ord">i</char> house, and into your<char style="ord">i</char> bedchamber, and upon your<char style="ord">i</char> bed, and into the house of your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and upon your<char style="ord">i</char> people, and into your<char style="ord">i</char> ovens, and into your<char style="ord">i</char> kneading troughs:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the frogs shall come up both on you<char style="ord">i</char>, and upon you<char style="ord">i</char> people, and upon all you<char style="ord">i</char> servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Say unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Stretch forth you<char style="ord">i</char> hand with you<char style="ord">i</char> rod over the streams, over the rivers, and over the ponds, and cause frogs to come up upon the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> stretched out his hand over the waters of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; and the frogs came up, and covered the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the magicians did so with their enchantments, and brought up frogs upon the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> called for Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and said, Intreat the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that he may take away the frogs from me, and from my people; and I will let the people go, that they may do sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, Glory over me: when shall I intreat for you<char style="ord">i</char>, and for you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and for you<char style="ord">i</char> people, to destroy the frogs from you<char style="ord">i</char> and you<char style="ord">i</char> houses, <char style="add">[that]</char> they may remain in the river only?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he said, Tomorrow. And he said, <char style="add">[Be it]</char> according to you<char style="ord">i</char> word: that you<char style="ord">i</char> may know that <char style="add">[there is]</char> none like unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the frogs shall depart from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and from you<char style="ord">i</char> houses, and from you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and from you<char style="ord">i</char> people; they shall remain in the river only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> went out from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> because of the frogs which he had brought against Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did according to the word of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>; and the frogs died out of the houses, out of the villages, and out of the fields.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they gathered them together upon heaps: and the land stank.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But when Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> saw that there was respite, he hardened his heart, and listened not unto them; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Say unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Stretch out you<char style="ord">i</char> rod, and strike the dust of the land, that it may become lice throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they did so; for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> stretched out his hand with his rod, and struck the dust of the earth, and it became lice in man, and in beast; all the dust of the land became lice throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the magicians did so with their enchantments to bring forth lice, but they could not: so there were lice upon man, and upon beast.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then the magicians said unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the finger of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart was hardened, and he listened not unto them; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Rise up early in the morning, and stand before Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>; lo, he comes forth to the water; and say unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Let my people go, that they may serve me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Else, if you<char style="ord">i</char> will not let my people go, behold, I will send swarms <char style="add">[of flies]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and upon you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and upon you<char style="ord">i</char> people, and into you<char style="ord">i</char> houses: and the houses of the Mitzri shall be full of swarms <char style="add">[of flies]</char>, and also the ground whereon they <char style="add">[are]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And I will sever in that day the land of Goshen <char style="add">[Drawing Near]</char>, in which my people dwell, that no swarms <char style="add">[of flies]</char> shall be there; to the end you<char style="ord">i</char> may know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the midst of the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And I will put a division between my people and you<char style="ord">i</char> people: tomorrow shall this sign be.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did so; and there came a grievous swarm <char style="add">[of flies]</char> into the house of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and <char style="add">[into]</char> his servants’ houses, and into all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: the land was corrupted by reason of the swarm <char style="add">[of flies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> called for Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and said, Go you<char style="ord">2f</char>, sacrifice to your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, It is not meet so to do; for we shall sacrifice the abomination of the Mitzri to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: lo, shall we sacrifice the abomination of the Mitzri before their eyes, and will they not stone us?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />We will go three days’ journey into the wilderness, and sacrifice to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, as he shall command us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> said, I will let you go, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may sacrifice to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in the wilderness; only you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not go very far away: intreat for me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, Behold, I go out from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will intreat the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that the swarms <char style="add">[of flies]</char> may depart from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, from his servants, and from his people, tomorrow: but let not Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> deal deceitfully any more in not letting the people go to sacrifice to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went out from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and entreated the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did according to the word of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>; and he removed the swarms <char style="add">[of flies]</char> from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, from his servants, and from his people; there remained not one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> hardened his heart at this time also, neither would he let the people go.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go in unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and tell him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char>, Let my people go, that they may serve me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For if you<char style="ord">i</char> refuse to let <char style="add">[them]</char> go, and will hold them still,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Behold, the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> is upon you<char style="ord">i</char> cattle which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the field, upon the horses, upon the asses, upon the camels, upon the oxen, and upon the sheep: <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> a very grievous murrain <char style="pn">(cattle disease; pestilence; plague)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall sever between the cattle of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and the cattle of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: and there shall nothing die of all <char style="add">[that is]</char> the children’s of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appointed a set time, saying, Tomorrow the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall do this thing in the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did that thing on the morrow, and all the cattle of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> died: but of the cattle of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> died not one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> sent, and, behold, there was not one of the cattle of the Yisra’eli’s dead. And the heart of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> was hardened, and he did not let the people go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Take to you handfuls of ashes of the furnace, and let Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> sprinkle it toward the heaven in the sight of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it shall become small dust in all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and shall be a boil breaking forth <char style="add">[with]</char> blisters upon man, and upon beast, throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they took ashes of the furnace, and stood before Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>; and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> sprinkled it up toward heaven; and it became a boil breaking forth <char style="add">[with]</char> blisters upon man, and upon beast.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the magicians could not stand before Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> because of the boils; for the boil was upon the magicians, and upon all the Mitzri.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> hardened the heart of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and he listened not unto them; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had spoken unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Rise up early in the morning, and stand before Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and say unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char>, Let my people go, that they may serve me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />For I will at this time send all my plagues upon you<char style="ord">i</char> heart, and upon you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and upon you<char style="ord">i</char> people; that you<char style="ord">i</char> may know that <char style="add">[there is]</char> none like me in all the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For now I will stretch out my hand, that I may strike you<char style="ord">i</char> and you<char style="ord">i</char> people with pestilence; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be cut off from the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And in very deed for this <char style="add">[cause]</char> have I raised you<char style="ord">i</char> up, for to show <char style="add">[in]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> my power; and that my name may be declared throughout all the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />As yet exalt you<char style="ord">i</char> yourself against my people, that you<char style="ord">i</char> will not let them go?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Behold, tomorrow about this time I will cause it to rain a very grievous hail, such as has not been in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> since the foundation thereof even until now.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Send therefore now, <char style="add">[and]</char> gather you<char style="ord">i</char> cattle, and all that you<char style="ord">i</char> have in the field; <char style="add">[for upon]</char> every man and beast which shall be found in the field, and shall not be brought home, the hail shall come down upon them, and they shall die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />He that feared the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> among the servants of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> made his servants and his cattle flee into the houses:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he that regarded not the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> left his servants and his cattle in the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Stretch forth you<char style="ord">i</char> hand toward heaven, that there may be hail in all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, upon man, and upon beast, and upon every herb of the field, throughout the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> stretched forth his rod toward heaven: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent thunder and hail, and the fire ran along upon the ground; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> rained hail upon the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />So there was hail, and fire mingled with the hail, very grievous, such as there was none like it in all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> since it became a nation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the hail struck throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> all that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the field, both man and beast; and the hail struck every herb of the field, and broke every tree of the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Only in the land of Goshen <char style="add">[Drawing Near]</char>, where the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [were]</char>, was there no hail.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> sent, and called for Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and said unto them, I have sinned this time: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> righteous, and I and my people <char style="add">[are]</char> wicked.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Intreat the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="pn">(for [it is] enough)</char> that there be no <char style="add">[more]</char> mighty thunderings and hail; and I will let you go, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall stay no longer.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto him, As soon as I am gone out of the city, I will spread abroad my hands unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; <char style="add">[and]</char> the thunder shall cease, neither shall there be any more hail; that you<char style="ord">i</char> may know how that the earth <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />But as for you<char style="ord">i</char> and you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, I know that you<char style="ord">2f</char> will not yet fear the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the flax and the barley was smitten: for the barley <char style="add">[was]</char> in the ear, and the flax <char style="add">[was]</char> blossomed <char style="pn">(in the seed or pod)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />But the wheat and the rye were not smitten: for they <char style="add">[were]</char> not grown up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went out of the city from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and spread abroad his hands unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and the thunders and hail ceased, and the rain was not poured upon the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And when Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> saw that the rain and the hail and the thunders were ceased, he sinned yet more, and hardened his heart, he and his servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the heart of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> was hardened, neither would he let the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had spoken by Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go in unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>: for I have hardened his heart, and the heart of his servants, that I might show these my signs before him:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And that you<char style="ord">i</char> may tell in the ears of you<char style="ord">i</char> son, and of you<char style="ord">i</char> son’s son, what things I have wrought in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and my signs which I have done among them; that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may know how that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> came in unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and said unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char>, How long will you<char style="ord">i</char> refuse to humble yourself before me? let my people go, that they may serve me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Else, if you<char style="ord">i</char> refuse to let my people go, behold, tomorrow will I bring the locusts into you<char style="ord">i</char> coast:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they shall cover the face of the earth, that one cannot be able to see the earth: and they shall eat the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of that which is escaped, which remains unto you from the hail, and shall eat every tree which grows for you out of the field:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they shall fill you<char style="ord">i</char> houses, and the houses of all you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and the houses of all the Mitzri; which neither you<char style="ord">i</char> fathers, nor you<char style="ord">i</char> fathers’ fathers have seen, since the day that they were upon the earth unto this day. And he turned himself, and went out from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> servants said unto him, How long shall this man be a snare unto us? let the men go, that they may serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: know you<char style="ord">i</char> not yet that Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> is destroyed?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> were brought again unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>: and he said unto them, Go, serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: <char style="add">[but]</char> who <char style="add">[are]</char> they that shall go?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, We will go with our young and with our old, with our sons and with our daughters, with our flocks and with our herds will we go; for we <char style="add">[must hold]</char> a feast unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he said unto them, Let the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be so with you, as I will let you go, and your little ones: look <char style="add">[to it]</char>; for evil <char style="add">[is]</char> before you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Not so: go now you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[that are]</char> men, and serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for that you<char style="ord">2f</char> did desire. And they were driven out from Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> presence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Stretch out you<char style="ord">i</char> hand over the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> for the locusts, that they may come up upon the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and eat every herb of the land, <char style="add">[even]</char> all that the hail has left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> stretched forth his rod over the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought an east wind upon the land all that day, and all <char style="add">[that]</char> night; <char style="add">[and]</char> when it was morning, the east wind brought the locusts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the locusts went up over all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and rested in all the coasts of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: very grievous <char style="add">[were they]</char>; before them there were no such locusts as they, neither after them shall be such.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For they covered the face of the whole earth, so that the land was darkened; and they did eat every herb of the land, and all the fruit of the trees which the hail had left: and there remained not any green thing in the trees, or in the herbs of the field, through all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> called for Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> in haste; and he said, I have sinned against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and against you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Now therefore forgive, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, my sin only this once, and intreat the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that he may take away from me this death only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he went out from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and entreated the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> turned a mighty strong west wind, which took away the locusts, and cast them into the Red sea; there remained not one locust in all the coasts of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> hardened Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart, so that he would not let the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Stretch out you<char style="ord">i</char> hand toward heaven, that there may be darkness over the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, even darkness <char style="add">[which]</char> may be felt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> stretched forth his hand toward heaven; and there was a thick darkness in all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> three days:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />They saw not one another, neither rose any from his place for three days: but all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had light in their dwellings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> called unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and said, Go you<char style="ord">2f</char>, serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; only let your flocks and your herds be detained <char style="pn">(held)</char>: let your little ones also go with you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, you<char style="ord">i</char> must give us also sacrifices and burnt offerings, that we may sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Our cattle also shall go with us; there shall not an hoof be left behind; for thereof must we take to serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and we know not with what we must serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, until we come there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> hardened Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart, and he would not let them go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> said unto him, Get you<char style="ord">i</char> from me, take heed to yourself, see my face no more; for in <char style="add">[that]</char> day you<char style="ord">i</char> see my face you<char style="ord">i</char> shall die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken well, I will see you<char style="ord">i</char> face again no more.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Yet will I bring one plague <char style="add">[more]</char> upon Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and upon Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; afterwards he will let you go hence: when he shall let <char style="add">[you]</char> go, he shall surely thrust you out hence altogether.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Speak now in the ears of the people, and let every man borrow of his neighbour, and every woman of her neighbour, jewels of silver, and jewels of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> gave the people favour in the sight of the Mitzri. Moreover the man Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters] [was]</char> very great in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, in the sight of Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> servants, and in the sight of the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, About midnight will I go out into the midst of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And all the firstborn in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> shall die, from the firstborn of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> that sits upon his throne, even unto the firstborn of the maidservant that <char style="add">[is]</char> behind the mill; and all the firstborn of beasts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And there shall be a great cry throughout all the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, such as there was none like it, nor shall be like it any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But against any of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall not a dog move his tongue, against man or beast: that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may know how that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> does put a difference between the Mitzri and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And all these you<char style="ord">i</char> servants shall come down unto me, and bow down themselves unto me, saying, Get you<char style="ord">i</char> out, and all the people that follow you<char style="ord">i</char>: and after that I will go out. And he went out from Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> in a great anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> shall not hearken unto you; that my wonders may be multiplied in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> did all these wonders before Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> hardened Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart, so that he would not let the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go out of his land.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />This month <char style="add">[shall be]</char> unto you the beginning of months: it <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the first month of the year to you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Speak you<char style="ord">2f</char> unto all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, In the tenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of this month they shall take to them every man a lamb, according to the house of <char style="add">[their]</char> fathers, a lamb for an house:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And if the household be too little for the lamb, let him and his neighbour next unto his house take <char style="add">[it]</char> according to the number of the souls; every man according to his eating shall make your count for the lamb.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Your lamb shall be without blemish, a male of the first year: you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall take <char style="add">[it]</char> out from the sheep, or from the goats:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall keep it up until the fourteenth day of the same month: and the whole assembly of the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall kill it in the evening.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And they shall take of the blood, and strike <char style="add">[it]</char> on the two side posts and on the upper doorpost of the houses, wherein they shall eat it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they shall eat the flesh in that night, roast with fire, and unleavened bread; <char style="add">[and]</char> with bitter <char style="add">[herbs]</char> they shall eat it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Eat not of it raw, nor coocked <char style="pn">(boiled)</char> at all with water, but roast <char style="add">[with]</char> fire; his head with his legs, and with the pertinence thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall let nothing of it remain until the morning; and that which remains of it until the morning you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall burn with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> eat it; <char style="add">[with]</char> your waist girded, your shoes on your feet, and your staff in your hand; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat it in haste: it <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah’s [Messiah Pre-Incarnate’s] Passover.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />For I will pass through the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> this night, and will strike all the firstborn in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, both man and beast; and against all the gods of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> I will execute judgment: I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the blood shall be to you for a token upon the houses where you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char>: and when I see the blood, I will pass over you, and the plague shall not be upon you to destroy <char style="add">[you]</char>, when I strike the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And this day shall be unto you for a memorial; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall keep it a feast to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> throughout your generations; you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall keep it a feast by an ordinance forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Seven days shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> eat unleavened bread; even the first day you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall put away leaven out of your houses: for whosoever eats leavened bread from the first day until the seventh day, that soul shall be cut off from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And in the first day <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> an holy convocation, and in the seventh day there shall be an holy convocation to you; no manner of work shall be done in them, save <char style="add">[that]</char> which every man must eat, that only may be done of you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall observe <char style="add">[the feast of]</char> unleavened bread; for in this selfsame day have I brought your armies out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: therefore shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> observe this day in your generations by an ordinance forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />In the first <char style="add">[month]</char>, on the fourteenth day of the month at even, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat unleavened bread, until the one and twentieth day of the month at even.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Seven days shall there be no leaven found in your houses: for whosoever eats that which is leavened, even that soul shall be cut off from the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whether he be a stranger, or born in the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat nothing leavened; in all your habitations shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> eat unleavened bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> called for all the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and said unto them, Draw out and take you a lamb according to your families, and kill the Passover.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall take a bunch of hyssop, and dip <char style="add">[it]</char> in the blood that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the basin, and strike the lintel <char style="pn">(top of the door frame)</char> and the two side posts with the blood that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the basin; and none of you shall go out at the door of his house until the morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will pass through to strike the Mitzri; and when he sees the blood upon the lintel <char style="pn">(top of the door frame)</char>, and on the two side posts, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will pass over the door, and will not suffer the destroyer to come in unto your houses to strike <char style="add">[you]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall observe this thing for an ordinance to you<char style="ord">i</char> and to you<char style="ord">i</char> sons forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, when you<char style="ord">2f</char> be come to the land which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will give you, according as he has promised, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall keep this service.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, when your children shall say unto you, What mean you<char style="ord">2f</char> by this service?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />That you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall say, It <char style="add">[is]</char> the sacrifice of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> Passover, who passed over the houses of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, when he struck the Mitzri, and delivered our houses. And the people bowed the head and worshipped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went away, and did as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, so did they.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And it came to pass, that at midnight the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck all the firstborn in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, from the firstborn of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> that sat on his throne unto the firstborn of the captive that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the dungeon; and all the firstborn of cattle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> rose up in the night, he, and all his servants, and all the Mitzri; and there was a great cry in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; for <char style="add">[there was]</char> not a house where <char style="add">[there was]</char> not one dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And he called for Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> by night, and said, Rise up, <char style="add">[and]</char> get you forth from among my people, both you<char style="ord">2f</char> and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and go, serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as you<char style="ord">2f</char> have said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Also take your flocks and your herds, as you<char style="ord">2f</char> have said, and be gone; and bless me also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the Mitzri were urgent upon the people, that they might send them out of the land in haste; for they said, We <char style="add">[be]</char> all dead <char style="add">[men]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the people took their dough before it was leavened, their kneading troughs being bound up in their clothes upon their shoulders.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did according to the word of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>; and they borrowed of the Mitzri jewels of silver, and jewels of gold, and clothing:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> gave the people favour in the sight of the Mitzri, so that they lent unto them <char style="add">[such things as they required]</char>. And they spoiled the Mitzri.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> journeyed from Ra’amses <char style="add">[Child of the Sun God]</char> to Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths] [Tabernacles/Booths]</char>, about six hundred thousand on foot <char style="add">[that were]</char> men, beside children.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And a mixed multitude went up also with them; and flocks, and herds, <char style="add">[even]</char> very much cattle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And they baked unleavened cakes of the dough which they brought forth out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, for it was not leavened; because they were thrust out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and could not wait, neither had they prepared for themselves any victual.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />Now the sojourning of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, who dwelt in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, <char style="add">[was]</char> four hundred and thirty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And it came to pass at the end of the four hundred and thirty years, even the selfsame day it came to pass, that all the hosts of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> went out from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />It <char style="add">[is]</char> a night to be much observed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for bringing them out from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: this <char style="add">[is]</char> that night of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to be observed of all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in their generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the ordinance of the Passover: There shall no stranger eat thereof:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />But every man’s servant that is bought for money, when you<char style="ord">i</char> have circumcised him, then shall he eat thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />A foreigner and an hired servant shall not eat thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />In one house shall it be eaten; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not carry forth ought of the flesh abroad out of the house; neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> break a bone thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />All the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall keep it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And when a stranger shall sojourn with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will keep the Passover to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, let all his males be circumcised, and then let him come near and keep it; and he shall be as one that is born in the land: for no uncircumcised person shall eat thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />One law shall be to him that is homeborn, and unto the stranger that sojourners among you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />Thus did all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, so did they.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />And it came to pass the selfsame day, <char style="add">[that]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did bring the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> by their armies.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> unto me all the firstborn, whatsoever opens the womb among the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[both]</char> of man and of beast: it <char style="add">[is]</char> my.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the people, Remember this day, in which you<char style="ord">2f</char> came out from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, out of the house of bondage; for by strength of hand the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought you out from this <char style="add">[place]</char>: there shall no leavened bread be eaten.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />This day came you<char style="ord">2f</char> out in the month Aviv.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it shall be when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall bring you<char style="ord">i</char> into the land of the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, and the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and the Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, which he swore unto you<char style="ord">i</char> fathers to give you<char style="ord">i</char>, a land flowing with milk and honey, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall keep this service in this month.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Seven days you<char style="ord">i</char> shall eat unleavened bread, and in the seventh day <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a feast to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Unleavened bread shall be eaten seven days; and there shall no leavened bread be seen with you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither shall there be leaven seen with you<char style="ord">i</char> in all you<char style="ord">i</char> quarters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall show you<char style="ord">i</char> son in that day, saying, <char style="add">[This is done]</char> because of that <char style="add">[which]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did unto me when I came forth out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it shall be for a sign unto you<char style="ord">i</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and for a memorial between you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, that the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> law may be in you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth: for with a strong hand has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought you<char style="ord">i</char> out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall therefore keep this ordinance in his season from year to year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it shall be when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall bring you<char style="ord">i</char> into the land of the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, as he swore unto you<char style="ord">i</char> and to you<char style="ord">i</char> fathers, and shall give it you<char style="ord">i</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />That you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set apart unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all that opens the womb, and every firstling that comes of a beast which you<char style="ord">i</char> have; the males <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And every firstling of an ass you<char style="ord">i</char> shall redeem with a lamb; and if you<char style="ord">i</char> will not redeem it, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall break his neck: and all the firstborn of man among you<char style="ord">i</char> children shall you<char style="ord">i</char> redeem.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And it shall be when your<char style="ord">i</char> son asks you<char style="ord">i</char> in time to come, saying, What <char style="add">[is]</char> this? that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say unto him, By strength of hand the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought us out from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, from the house of bondage:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> would hardly let us go, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> killed all the firstborn in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, both the firstborn of man, and the firstborn of beast: therefore I sacrifice to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all that opens the womb, being males; but all the firstborn of my children I redeem.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it shall be for a token upon you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and for frontlets between you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes: for by strength of hand the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought us forth out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> had let the people go, that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> led them not <char style="add">[through]</char> the way of the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, although that <char style="add">[was]</char> near; for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said, Lest perhaps the people repent when they see war, and they return to Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />But God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> led the people about, <char style="add">[through]</char> the way of the wilderness of the Red sea: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went up harnessed out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> took the bones of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char> with him: for he had straightly sworn the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> will surely visit you; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall carry up my bones away hence with you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And they took their journey from Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char>, and encamped in ‘Eitam <char style="add">[Lair of Wild Beasts] [with them: their plowshare]</char>, in the edge of the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light; to go by day and night:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />He took not away the pillar of the cloud by day, nor the pillar of fire by night, <char style="add">[from]</char> before the people.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Speak unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that they turn and encamp before Pi-Hachirot <char style="add">[The Place where the Sedge Grows]</char>, between Migdol <char style="add">[Tower]</char> and the sea, over against Ba’al-Tz’fon <char style="add">[Lord of the North]</char>: before it shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> encamp by the sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> will say of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, They <char style="add">[are]</char> entangled in the land, the wilderness has shut them in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And I will harden Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> heart, that he shall follow after them; and I will be honoured upon Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and upon all his host; that the Mitzri may know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And they did so.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it was told the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> that the people fled: and the heart of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> and of his servants was turned against the people, and they said, Why have we done this, that we have let Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go from serving us?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he made ready his chariot, and took his people with him:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he took six hundred chosen chariots, and all the chariots of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and captains over every one of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> hardened the heart of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and he pursued after the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went out with an high hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But the Mitzri pursued after them, all the horses <char style="add">[and]</char> chariots of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and his horsemen, and his army, and overtook them encamping by the sea, beside Pi-Hachirot <char style="add">[The Place where the Sedge Grows]</char>, before Ba’al-Tz’fon <char style="add">[Lord of the North]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And when Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> drew near, the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> lifted up their eyes, and, behold, the Mitzri marched after them; and they were sore afraid: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> cried out unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Because <char style="add">[there were]</char> no graves in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, have you<char style="ord">i</char> taken us away to die in the wilderness? wherefore have you<char style="ord">i</char> dealt thus with us, to carry us forth out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Is]</char> not this the word that we did tell you<char style="ord">i</char> in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, saying, Let us alone, that we may serve the Mitzri? For <char style="add">[it had been]</char> better for us to serve the Mitzri, than that we should die in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the people, Fear you<char style="ord">2f</char> not, stand still, and see the salvation of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he will show to you today: for the Mitzri whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> have seen today, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall see them again no more forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall fight for you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall hold your peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, For what reason do you<char style="ord">i</char> cry unto me? speak unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that they go forward:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But lift you<char style="ord">i</char> up you<char style="ord">i</char> rod, and stretch out you<char style="ord">i</char> hand over the sea, and divide it: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall go on dry <char style="add">[ground]</char> through the midst of the sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And I, behold, I will harden the hearts of the Mitzri, and they shall follow them: and I will get me honour upon Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and upon all his host, upon his chariots, and upon his horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the Mitzri shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I have gotten me honour upon Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, upon his chariots, and upon his horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which went before the camp of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, removed and went behind them; and the pillar of the cloud went from before their face, and stood behind them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And it came between the camp of the Mitzri and the camp of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and it was a cloud and darkness <char style="add">[to them]</char>, but it gave light by night <char style="add">[to these]</char>: so that the one came not near the other all the night.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> stretched out his hand over the sea; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> caused the sea to go <char style="add">[back]</char> by a strong east wind all that night, and made the sea dry <char style="add">[land]</char>, and the waters were divided.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went into the midst of the sea upon the dry <char style="add">[ground]</char>: and the waters <char style="add">[were]</char> a wall unto them on their right hand, and on their left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the Mitzri pursued, and went in after them to the midst of the sea, <char style="add">[even]</char> all Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> horses, his chariots, and his horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And it came to pass, that in the morning watch the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> looked unto the host of the Mitzri through the pillar of fire and of the cloud, and troubled the host of the Mitzri,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And took off their chariot wheels, that they drove them heavily: so that the Mitzri said, Let us flee from the face of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> fights for them against the Mitzri.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Stretch out you<char style="ord">i</char> hand over the sea, that the waters may come again upon the Mitzri, upon their chariots, and upon their horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> stretched forth his hand over the sea, and the sea returned to his strength when the morning appeared; and the Mitzri fled against it; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> overthrew the Mitzri in the midst of the sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the waters returned, and covered the chariots, and the horsemen, <char style="add">[and]</char> all the host of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> that came into the sea after them; there remained not so much as one of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />But the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> walked upon dry <char style="add">[land]</char> in the midst of the sea; and the waters <char style="add">[were]</char> a wall unto them on their right hand, and on their left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Thus the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> saved Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that day out of the hand of the Mitzri; and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw the Mitzri dead upon the sea shore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw that great work which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did upon the Mitzri: and the people feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and believed the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and his servant Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then sang Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> this song unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and spoke, saying, I will sing unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, for he has triumphed gloriously: the horse and his rider has he thrown into the sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The LORD-Yah <char style="add">[Behold The Hand]</char> <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> my strength and song, and he is become my salvation: he <char style="add">[is]</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and I will prepare him an habitation; my father’s God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and I will exalt him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> a man of war: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> his name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> chariots and his host has he cast into the sea: his chosen captains also are drowned in the Red sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />The depths have covered them: they sank into the bottom as a stone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />You<char style="ord">1s</char> right hand, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, is become glorious in power: you<char style="ord">i</char> right hand, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, has dashed in pieces the enemy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And in the greatness of your<char style="ord">i</char> excellency you<char style="ord">i</char> have overthrown them that rose up against you<char style="ord">i</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> sent forth your<char style="ord">i</char> wrath, <char style="add">[which]</char> consumed them as stubble.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And with the blast of you<char style="ord">i</char> nostrils the waters were gathered together, the floods stood upright as an heap, <char style="add">[and]</char> the depths were congealed in the heart of the sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The enemy said, I will pursue, I will overtake, I will divide the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>; my lust shall be satisfied upon them; I will draw my sword, my hand shall destroy them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> did blow with you<char style="ord">i</char> wind, the sea covered them: they sank as lead in the mighty waters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Who <char style="add">[is]</char> like unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, among the gods? who <char style="add">[is]</char> like you<char style="ord">i</char>, glorious in holiness, fearful <char style="add">[in]</char> praises, doing wonders?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> stretched out your<char style="ord">i</char> right hand, the earth swallow (to approve, commend, accept)ed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char> mercy have led forth the people <char style="add">[which]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have redeemed: you<char style="ord">i</char> have guided <char style="add">[them]</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char> strength unto you<char style="ord">i</char> holy habitation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The people shall hear, <char style="add">[and]</char> be afraid: sorrow shall take hold on the inhabitants of P’leshet <char style="add">[Land of Strangers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then the dukes of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> shall be amazed; the mighty men of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, trembling shall take hold upon them; all the inhabitants of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> shall melt away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Fear and dread shall fall upon them; by the greatness of you<char style="ord">i</char> arm they shall be <char style="add">[as]</char> still as a stone; till you<char style="ord">i</char> people pass over, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, till the people pass over, <char style="add">[which]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have purchased.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring them in, and plant them in the mountain of you<char style="ord">i</char> inheritance, <char style="add">[in]</char> the place, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[which]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have made for you<char style="ord">i</char> to dwell in, <char style="add">[in]</char> the Sanctuary, O Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Lord Above All Things]</char>, <char style="add">[which]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> hands have established.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall reign forever and ever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For the horse of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> went in with his chariots and with his horsemen into the sea, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought again the waters of the sea upon them; but the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went on dry <char style="add">[land]</char> in the midst of the sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Miryam <char style="add">[rebellion]</char> the prophetess, the sister of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, took a timbrel in her hand; and all the women went out after her with timbrels and with dances.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Miryam <char style="add">[rebellion]</char> answered them, Sing you<char style="ord">2f</char> to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, for he has triumphed gloriously; the horse and his rider has he thrown into the sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> brought Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the Red sea, and they went out into the wilderness of Shur <char style="add">[wall]</char>; and they went three days in the wilderness, and found no water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And when they came to Marah <char style="add">[Bitterness]</char>, they could not drink of the waters of Marah <char style="add">[Bitterness]</char>, for they <char style="add">[were]</char> bitter: therefore the name of it was called Marah <char style="add">[Bitterness]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the people murmured against Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying, What shall we drink?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And he cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> showed him a tree, <char style="add">[which]</char> when he had cast into the waters, the waters were made sweet: there he made for them a statute and an ordinance, and there he proved them,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And said, If you<char style="ord">i</char> will diligently hearken to the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and will do that which is right in his sight, and will give ear to his commandments, and keep all his statutes, I will put none of these diseases upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, which I have brought upon the Mitzri: for I <char style="add">[am]</char> Yehovah Rof’ekha <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate that heals you]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And they came to Eilim <char style="add">[Palms]</char>, where <char style="add">[were]</char> twelve wells of water, and threescore and ten palm trees: and they encamped there by the waters.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And they took their journey from Eilim <char style="add">[Palms]</char>, and all the congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came unto the wilderness of Sin, which <char style="add">[is]</char> between Eilim <char style="add">[Palms]</char> and Sinai, on the fifteenth day of the second month after their departing out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the whole congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> murmured against Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> in the wilderness:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto them, Would to God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> we had died by the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, when we sat by the flesh pots, <char style="add">[and]</char> when we did eat bread to the full; for you<char style="ord">2f</char> have brought us forth into this wilderness, to kill this whole assembly with hunger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then said the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Behold, I will rain bread from heaven for you; and the people shall go out and gather a certain rate every day, that I may prove them, whether they will walk in my law, or no.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, that on the sixth day they shall prepare <char style="add">[that]</char> which they bring in; and it shall be twice as much as they gather daily.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> said unto all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, At even, then you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has brought you out from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And in the morning, then you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall see the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for that he hears your murmurings against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and what <char style="add">[are]</char> we, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> murmur against us?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, <char style="add">[This shall be]</char>, when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall give you in the evening flesh to eat, and in the morning bread to the full; for that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> hears your murmurings which you<char style="ord">2f</char> murmur against him: and what <char style="add">[are]</char> we? your murmurings <char style="add">[are]</char> not against us, but against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> spoke unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Say unto all the congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Come near before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for he has heard your murmurings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And it came to pass, as Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> spoke unto the whole congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that they looked toward the wilderness, and, behold, the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared in the cloud.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />I have heard the murmurings of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: speak unto them, saying, At even you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat flesh, and in the morning you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be filled with bread; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And it came to pass, that at even the quails came up, and covered the camp: and in the morning the dew lay round about the host.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when the dew that lay was gone up, behold, upon the face of the wilderness <char style="add">[there lay]</char> a small round thing, <char style="add">[as]</char> small as the grey frost on the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, they said one to another, It <char style="add">[is]</char> manna: for they did not know what it <char style="add">[was]</char>. And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto them, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the bread which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has given you to eat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has commanded, Gather of it every man according to his eating, an omer for every man, <char style="add">[according to]</char> the number of your persons; take you<char style="ord">2f</char> every man for <char style="add">[them]</char> which <char style="add">[are]</char> in his tents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did so, and gathered, some more, some less.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when they did measure <char style="pn">(deal out)</char> <char style="add">[it]</char> with an omer, he that gathered much had nothing over, and he that gathered little had no lack; they gathered every man according to his eating.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, Let no man leave of it till the morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Yet they listened not unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>; but some of them left of it until the morning, and it bred worms, and stank: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> was exceedingly angry with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they gathered it every morning, every man according to his eating: and when the sun waxed hot, it melted.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> on the sixth day they gathered twice as much bread, two omers for one <char style="add">[man]</char>: and all the rulers of the congregation came and told Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he said unto them, This <char style="add">[is that]</char> which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has said, Tomorrow <char style="add">[is]</char> the rest of the Holy Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: bake <char style="add">[that]</char> which you<char style="ord">2f</char> will bake <char style="add">[today]</char>, and seethe that you<char style="ord">2f</char> will seethe; and that which remains over lay up for you to be kept until the morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And they laid it up till the morning, as Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> bade: and it did not stink, neither was there any worm in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, Eat that today; for today <char style="add">[is]</char> a Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: today you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not find it in the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Six days you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall gather it; but on the seventh day, <char style="add">[which is]</char> the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, in it there shall be none.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> there went out <char style="add">[some]</char> of the people on the seventh day for to gather, and they found none.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, How long refuse you<char style="ord">2f</char> to keep my commandments and my laws?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />See, for that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has given you the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, therefore he gives you on the sixth day the bread of two days; abide you<char style="ord">2f</char> every man in his place, let no man go out of his place on the seventh day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />So the people rested on the seventh day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> called the name thereof Manna: and it <char style="add">[was]</char> like coriander seed, white; and the taste of it <char style="add">[was]</char> like wafers <char style="add">[made]</char> with honey.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commands, Fill an omer of it to be kept for your generations; that they may see the bread which I have fed you in the wilderness, when I brought you forth from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Take a pot, and put an omer full of manna in it, and lay it up before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to be kept for your generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />As the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, so Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> laid it up before the Testimony, to be kept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did eat manna forty years, until they came to a land inhabited; they did eat manna, until they came unto the borders of the land of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Now an omer <char style="add">[is]</char> the tenth <char style="add">[part]</char> of an eifah.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And all the congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> journeyed from the wilderness of Sin, after their journeys, according to the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and pitched in Refidim <char style="add">[Resting Places]</char>: and <char style="add">[there was]</char> no water for the people to drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For what reason the people did quarrel with Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and said, Give us water that we may drink. And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto them, Why quarrel you<char style="ord">2f</char> with me? wherefore do you<char style="ord">2f</char> tempt the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the people thirsted there for water; and the people murmured against Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and said, For what reason <char style="add">[is]</char> this <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought us up out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, to kill us and our children and our cattle with thirst?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, What shall I do unto this people? they be almost ready to stone me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go on before the people, and take with you<char style="ord">i</char> of the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and your<char style="ord">i</char> rod, which you<char style="ord">i</char> stuck the river, take in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Behold, I will stand before you<char style="ord">i</char> there upon the rock in Horev <char style="add">[Desert]</char>; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall strike the rock, and there shall come water out of it, that the people may drink. And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> did so in the sight of the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he called the name of the place Massah <char style="add">[Testing]</char>, and M’rivah <char style="add">[Arguing]</char>, because of the chiding of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and because they tempted the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Is the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> among us, or not?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then came ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>, and fought with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Refidim <char style="add">[Resting Places]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, Choose us out men, and go out, fight with ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>: tomorrow I will stand on the top of the hill with the rod of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in my hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> did as Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> had said to him, and fought with ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char> went up to the top of the hill.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> held up his hand, that Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> prevailed: and when he let down his hand, ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char> prevailed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ hands <char style="add">[were]</char> heavy; and they took a stone, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> under him, and he sat thereon; and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char> detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> up his hands, the one on the one side, and the other on the other side; and his hands were steady until the going down of the sun.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> scattered <char style="pn">(defeated in battle)</char> ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char> and his people with the edge of the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Write this <char style="add">[for]</char> a memorial in a book, and rehearse <char style="add">[it]</char> in the ears of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>: for I will utterly put out the remembrance of ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char> from under heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> built an altar, and called the name of it Yehovah-Nissi <char style="add">[God is My Banner/Miracle]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For he said, Because the LORD-Yah <char style="add">[Behold The Hand]</char> <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sworn <char style="add">[that]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[will have]</char> war with ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char> from generation to generation.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />When Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char>, the priest of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law, heard of all that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had done for Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> his people, <char style="add">[and]</char> that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had brought Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char>, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law, took Zipporah, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ wife, after he had sent her back,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And her two sons; of which the name of the one <char style="add">[was]</char> Gershom <char style="add">[Exiled One]</char>; for he said, I have been an alien in a strange land:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the name of the other <char style="add">[was]</char> Eli’ezer <char style="add">[God is help]</char>; for the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of my father, <char style="add">[said he, was]</char> my help, and delivered me from the sword of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char>, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law, came with his sons and his wife unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> into the wilderness, where he encamped at the mount of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, I you<char style="ord">i</char> father in law Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char> am come unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> wife, and her two sons with her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went out to meet his father in law, and did obesiance <char style="pn">(bowing or kneeling in respect)</char>, and kissed him; and they asked each other of <char style="add">[their]</char> welfare; and they came into the tent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> told his father in law all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had done unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> and to the Mitzri for Yisra’el’s <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sake, <char style="add">[and]</char> all the travail that had come upon them by the way, and <char style="add">[how]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char> rejoiced for all the goodness which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had done to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whom he had delivered out of the hand of the Mitzri.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char> said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, who has delivered you out of the hand of the Mitzri, and out of the hand of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, who has delivered the people from under the hand of the Mitzri.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Now I know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> greater than all gods: for in the thing wherein they dealt proudly <char style="add">[he was]</char> above them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Yitro <char style="add">[Excellence]</char>, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law, took a burnt offering and sacrifices for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> came, and all the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to eat bread with Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law before God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, that Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> sat to judge the people: and the people stood by Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> from the morning unto the evening.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law saw all that he did to the people, he said, What <char style="add">[is]</char> this thing that you<char style="ord">i</char> do to the people? why sit you<char style="ord">i</char> yourself alone, and all the people stand by you<char style="ord">i</char> from morning unto even?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto his father in law, Because the people come unto me to enquire of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />When they have a matter, they come unto me; and I judge between one and another, and I do make <char style="add">[them]</char> know the statutes of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and his laws.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ father in law said unto him, The thing that you<char style="ord">i</char> do <char style="add">[is]</char> not good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> will surely wear away, both you<char style="ord">i</char>, and this people that <char style="add">[is]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>: for this thing <char style="add">[is]</char> too heavy for you<char style="ord">i</char>; you<char style="ord">i</char> are not able to perform it yourself alone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Listen now unto my voice, I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> counsel, and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shall be with you<char style="ord">i</char>: Be you<char style="ord">i</char> for the people to God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> -ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may bring the causes unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall teach them ordinances and laws, and shall show them the way wherein they must walk, and the work that they must do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Moreover you<char style="ord">i</char> shall provide out of all the people able men, such as fear God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, men of truth, hating covetousness; and place <char style="add">[such]</char> over them, <char style="add">[to be]</char> rulers of thousands, <char style="add">[and]</char> rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And let them judge the people at all seasons: and it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> every great matter they shall bring unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, but every small matter they shall judge: so shall it be easier for yourself, and they shall bear <char style="add">[the burden]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do this thing, and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> command you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[so]</char>, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be able to endure, and all this people shall also go to their place in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />So Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> listened to the voice of his father in law, and did all that he had said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> chose able men out of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and made them heads over the people, rulers of thousands, rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And they judged the people at all seasons: the hard causes they brought unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, but every small matter they judged themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> let his father in law depart; and he went his way into his own land.</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the third month, when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were gone forth out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, the same day came they <char style="add">[into]</char> the wilderness of Sinai.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For they were departed from Refidim <char style="add">[Resting Places]</char>, and were come <char style="add">[to]</char> the desert of Sinai, and had pitched in the wilderness; and there Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> camped before the mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went up unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> called unto him out of the mountain, saying, Thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say to the house of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, and tell the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> have seen what I did unto the Mitzri, and <char style="add">[how]</char> I bore you on eagles’ wings, and brought you unto myself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Now therefore, if you<char style="ord">2f</char> will obey my voice indeed, and keep my covenant, then you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be a peculiar <char style="pn">(particular; special; one’s own)</char> treasure unto me above all people: for all the earth <char style="add">[is]</char> my:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be unto me a kingdom of priests, and an holy nation. These <char style="add">[are]</char> the words which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> came and called for the elders of the people, and laid before their faces all these words which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And all the people answered together, and said, All that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken we will do. And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> returned the words of the people unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Lo, I come unto you<char style="ord">i</char> in a thick cloud, that the people may hear when I speak with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and believe you<char style="ord">i</char> forever. And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> told the words of the people unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go unto the people, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> them today and tomorrow, and let them wash their clothes,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And be ready against the third day: for the third day the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will come down in the sight of all the people upon mount Sinai.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set bounds unto the people round about, saying, Take heed to yourselves, <char style="add">[that you<char style="ord">2f</char>]</char> go <char style="add">[not]</char> up into the mount, or touch the border of it: whosoever touches the mount shall be surely put to death:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />There shall not an hand touch it, but he shall surely be stoned, or shot through; whether <char style="add">[it be]</char> beast or man, it shall not live: when the trumpet sounds long, they shall come up to the mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went down from the mount unto the people, and sanctified the people; and they washed their clothes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said unto the people, Be ready against the third day: come not at <char style="add">[your]</char> wives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass on the third day in the morning, that there were thunders and lightnings, and a thick cloud upon the mount, and the voice of the trumpet exceeding loud; so that all the people that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the camp trembled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> brought forth the people out of the camp to meet with God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and they stood at the lower part of the mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And mount Sinai was altogether on a smoke, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> descended upon it in fire: and the smoke thereof ascended as the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mount quaked greatly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And when the voice of the trumpet sounded long, and waxed louder and louder, Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> spoke, and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> answered him by a voice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came down upon mount Sinai, on the top of the mount: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> called Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters] [up]</char> to the top of the mount; and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go down, charge the people, lest they break through unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to gaze, and many of them perish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And let the priests also, which come near to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> themselves, lest the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> break forth upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, The people cannot come up to mount Sinai: for you<char style="ord">i</char> charged us, saying, Set bounds about the mount, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Away, get you<char style="ord">i</char> down, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come up, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>: but let not the priests and the people break through to come up unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, lest he break forth upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />So Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went down unto the people, and spoke unto them.</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> spoke all these words, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which have brought you<char style="ord">i</char> out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, out of the house of bondage.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall have no other gods before me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not make unto you<char style="ord">i</char> any graven image, or any likeness <char style="add">[of anything]</char> that <char style="add">[is]</char> in heaven above, or that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the earth beneath, or that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the water under the earth:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not bow down yourself to them, nor serve them: for I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [am]</char> El Kana <char style="add">[a jealous God]</char>, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth <char style="add">[generation]</char> of them that hate me;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And showing mercy unto thousands of them that love me, and keep my commandments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not take the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in vain; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will not hold him guiltless that takes his name in vain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Remember the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day, to keep it holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Six days shall you<char style="ord">i</char> labour, and do all you<char style="ord">i</char> work:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But the seventh day <char style="add">[is]</char> the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: <char style="add">[in it]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not do any work, you<char style="ord">i</char>, nor you<char style="ord">i</char> son, nor you<char style="ord">i</char> daughter, you<char style="ord">i</char> manservant, nor you<char style="ord">i</char> maidservant, nor you<char style="ord">i</char> cattle, nor you<char style="ord">i</char> stranger that <char style="add">[is]</char> within you<char style="ord">i</char> gates:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For <char style="add">[in]</char> six days the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that in them <char style="add">[is]</char>, and rested the seventh day: wherefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day, and consecrated it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Honour you<char style="ord">i</char> father and you<char style="ord">i</char> mother: that you<char style="ord">i</char> days may be long upon the land which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> gives you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not kill.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not commit adultery.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not steal.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not bear false witness against you<char style="ord">i</char> neighbour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not covet you<char style="ord">i</char> neighbour’s house, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not covet your<char style="ord">i</char> neighbour’s wife, nor his manservant, nor his maidservant, nor his ox, nor his ass, nor anything that <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> neighbour’s.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And all the people saw the thunderings, and the lightnings, and the noise of the trumpet, and the mountain smoking: and when the people saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, they removed, and stood afar off.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Speak you<char style="ord">i</char> with us, and we will hear: but let not God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> speak with us, lest we die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the people, Fear not: for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> is come to prove you, and that his fear may be before your faces, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> sin not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the people stood afar off, and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> drew near unto the thick darkness where God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Thus you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> have seen that I have talked with you from heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not make with me gods of silver, neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> make unto you gods of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />An altar of earth you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make unto me, and shall sacrifice thereon you<char style="ord">i</char> burnt offerings, and you<char style="ord">i</char> peace offerings, you<char style="ord">i</char> sheep, and you<char style="ord">i</char> oxen: in all places where I record my name I will come unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will bless you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And if you<char style="ord">i</char> will make me an altar of stone, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not build it of cut stone: for if you<char style="ord">i</char> lift up you<char style="ord">i</char> tool upon it, you<char style="ord">i</char> have polluted it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Neither shall you<char style="ord">i</char> go up by steps unto my altar, that you<char style="ord">i</char> nakedness be not discovered thereon.</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> the judgments which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> buy an ‘Evri’ot <char style="add">[Hebrew]</char> servant, six years he shall serve: and in the seventh he shall go out free for nothing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />If he came in by himself, he shall go out by himself: if he were married, then his wife shall go out with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />If his master have given him a wife, and she have born him sons or daughters; the wife and her children shall be her master’s, and he shall go out by himself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And if the servant shall plainly say, I love my master, my wife, and my children; I will not go out free:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then his master shall bring him unto the judges; he shall also bring him to the door, or unto the door post; and his master shall bore his ear through with an aul; and he shall serve him forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And if a man sell his daughter to be a maidservant, she shall not go out as the menservants do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />If she please not her master, who has betrothed her to himself, then shall he let her be redeemed: to sell her unto a strange nation he shall have no power, seeing he has dealt deceitfully with her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And if he have betrothed her unto his son, he shall deal with her after the manner of daughters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />If he take him another <char style="add">[wife]</char>; her food, her clothing, and her duty of marriage, shall he not diminish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And if he do not these three unto her, then shall she go out free without money.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />He that smites a man, so that he die, shall be surely put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And if a man lie not in wait, but God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> deliver <char style="add">[him]</char> into his hand; then I will appoint you<char style="ord">i</char> a place to which he shall flee.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But if a man come presumptuously upon his neighbour, to slay him with deceit; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take him from my altar, that he may die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he that smites his father, or his mother, shall be surely put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he that steals a man, and sells him, or if he be found in his hand, he shall surely be put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he that curses his father, or his mother, shall surely be put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And if men strive together, and one strike another with a stone, or with <char style="add">[his]</char> fist, and he die not, but keeps <char style="add">[his]</char> bed:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />If he rise again, and walk abroad upon his staff, then shall he that struck <char style="add">[him]</char> be quit <char style="pn">(acquitted; found not guilty)</char>: only he shall pay <char style="add">[for]</char> the loss of his time, and shall cause <char style="add">[him]</char> to be thoroughly healed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And if a man strike his servant, or his maid, with a rod, and he die under his hand; he shall be surely punished.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Yet, if he continue a day or two, he shall not be punished: for he <char style="add">[is]</char> his money.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />If men strive, and hurt a woman with child, so that her fruit depart <char style="add">[from her]</char>, and yet no mischief follow: he shall be surely punished, according as the woman’s husband will lay upon him; and he shall pay as the <char style="add">[determine]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And if <char style="add">[any]</char> mischief follow, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall give life for life,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand, foot for foot,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Burning for burning, wound for wound, stripe for stripe.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And if a man strike the eye of his servant, or the eye of his maid, that it perish; he shall let him go free for his eye’s sake.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And if he strike out his manservant’s tooth, or his maidservant’s tooth; he shall let him go free for his tooth’s sake.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />If an ox gore a man or a woman, that they die: then the ox shall be surely stoned, and his flesh shall not be eaten; but the owner of the ox <char style="add">[shall be]</char> quit <char style="pn">(acquitted; found not guilty)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />But if the ox were wont <char style="pn">(used to; in the habit of)</char> to push with his horn in time past, and it has been testified to his owner, and he has not kept him in, but that he has killed a man or a woman; the ox shall be stoned, and his owner also shall be put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />If there be laid on him a sum of money, then he shall give for the ransom of his life whatsoever is laid upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Whether he have gored a son, or have gored a daughter, according to this judgment shall it be done unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />If the ox shall push a manservant or a maidservant; he shall give unto their master thirty shekels of silver, and the ox shall be stoned.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And if a man shall open a pit, or if a man shall dig a pit, and not cover it, and an ox or an ass fall in it;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />The owner of the pit shall make <char style="add">[it]</char> good, <char style="add">[and]</char> give money unto the owner of them; and the dead <char style="add">[beast]</char> shall be his.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And if one man’s ox hurt another’s, that he die; then they shall sell the live ox, and divide the money of it; and the dead <char style="add">[ox]</char> also they shall divide.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Or if it be known that the ox has used to push in time past, and his owner has not kept him in; he shall surely pay ox for ox; and the dead shall be his own.</para>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />If a man shall steal an ox, or a sheep, and kill it, or sell it; he shall restore five oxen for an ox, and four sheep for a sheep.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />If a thief be found breaking up, and be smitten that he die, <char style="add">[there shall]</char> no blood <char style="add">[be shed]</char> for him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />If the sun be risen upon him, <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> blood <char style="add">[shed]</char> for him; <char style="add">[for]</char> he should make full restitution; if he have nothing, then he shall be sold for his theft.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />If the theft be certainly found in his hand alive, whether it be ox, or ass, or sheep; he shall restore double.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />If a man shall cause a field or vineyard to be eaten, and shall put in his beast, and shall feed in another man’s field; of the best of his own field, and of the best of his own vineyard, shall he make restitution.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />If fire break out, and catch in thorns, so that the stacks of corn, or the standing corn, or the field, be consumed <char style="add">[with that]</char>; he that kindled the fire shall surely make restitution.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />If a man shall deliver unto his neighbour money or stuff to keep, and it be stolen out of the man’s house; if the thief be found, let him pay double.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />If the thief be not found, then the master of the house shall be brought unto the judges, <char style="add">[to see]</char> whether he have put his hand unto his neighbour’s goods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For all manner of trespass, <char style="add">[whether it be]</char> for ox, for ass, for sheep, for clothing, <char style="add">[or]</char> for any manner of lost thing, which <char style="add">[another]</char> challenges to be his, the cause of both parties shall come before the judges; <char style="add">[and]</char> whom the shall condemn, he shall pay double unto his neighbour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />If a man deliver unto his neighbour an ass, or an ox, or a sheep, or any beast, to keep; and it die, or be hurt, or driven away, no man seeing <char style="add">[it]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Then]</char> shall an oath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be between them both, that he has not put his hand unto his neighbour’s goods; and the owner of it shall accept <char style="add">[thereof]</char>, and he shall not make <char style="add">[it]</char> good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And if it be stolen from him, he shall make restitution unto the owner thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />If it be torn in pieces, <char style="add">[then]</char> let him bring it <char style="add">[for]</char> witness, <char style="add">[and]</char> he shall not make good that which was torn.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And if a man borrow <char style="add">[ought]</char> of his neighbour, and it be hurt, or die, the owner thereof <char style="add">[being]</char> not with it, he shall surely make <char style="add">[it]</char> good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[But]</char> if the owner thereof <char style="add">[be]</char> with it, he shall not make <char style="add">[it]</char> good: if it <char style="add">[be]</char> an hired <char style="add">[thing]</char>, it came for his hire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And if a man entice a maid that is not betrothed, and lie with her, he shall surely endow her to be his wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />If her father utterly refuse to give her unto him, he shall pay money according to the dowry of virgins.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not suffer a witch to live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Whosoever lies with a beast shall surely be put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />He that sacrifices unto <char style="add">[any]</char> god, save unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> only, he shall be utterly destroyed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall neither vex a stranger, nor oppress him: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> were strangers in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not afflict any widow, or fatherless child.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> afflict them in any wise, and they cry at all unto me, I will surely hear their cry;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And my wrath shall grow <char style="pn">(become; advance)</char> hot, and I will kill you with the sword; and your wives shall be widows, and your children fatherless.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> lend money to <char style="add">[any of]</char> my people <char style="add">[that is]</char> poor by you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not be to him as an usurer, neither shall you<char style="ord">i</char> lay upon him usury <char style="pn">(interest paid for using money)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> at all take you<char style="ord">i</char> neighbour’s clothing to pledge, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall deliver it unto him by that the sun goes down:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />For that <char style="add">[is]</char> his covering only, it <char style="add">[is]</char> his clothing for his skin: wherein shall he sleep? and it shall come to pass, when he cries unto me, that I will hear; for I <char style="add">[am]</char> gracious.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not revile the gods, nor curse the ruler of you<char style="ord">i</char> people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not delay <char style="add">[to offer]</char> the first of you<char style="ord">i</char> ripe fruits, and of you<char style="ord">i</char> liquors: the firstborn of you<char style="ord">i</char> sons shall you<char style="ord">i</char> give unto me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Likewise shall you<char style="ord">i</char> do with you<char style="ord">i</char> oxen, <char style="add">[and]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> sheep: seven days it shall be with his mother; on the eighth day you<char style="ord">i</char> shall give it me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be holy men unto me: neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> eat <char style="add">[any]</char> flesh <char style="add">[that is]</char> torn of beasts in the field; you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall cast it to the dogs.</para>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not raise a false report: put not you<char style="ord">i</char> hand with the wicked to be an unrighteous witness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not follow a multitude to <char style="add">[do]</char> evil; neither shall you<char style="ord">i</char> speak in a cause to decline after many to wrest <char style="add">[judgment]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Neither shall you<char style="ord">i</char> Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char> a poor man in his cause.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> meet you<char style="ord">i</char> enemy’s ox or his ass going astray, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely bring it back to him again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> see the ass of him that hates you<char style="ord">i</char> lying under his burden, and would refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char> to help him, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely help with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not wrest the judgment of you<char style="ord">i</char> poor in his cause.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Keep you<char style="ord">i</char> far from a false matter; and the innocent and righteous slay you<char style="ord">i</char> not: for I will not justify the wicked.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take no gift: for the gift blinds the wise, and perverts the words of the righteous.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Also you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not oppress a stranger: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> know the heart of a stranger, seeing you<char style="ord">2f</char> were strangers in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And six years you<char style="ord">i</char> shall sow you<char style="ord">i</char> land, and shall gather in the fruits thereof:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But the seventh <char style="add">[year]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall let it rest and lie still; that the poor of you<char style="ord">i</char> people may eat: and what they leave the beasts of the field shall eat. In like manner you<char style="ord">i</char> shall deal with you<char style="ord">i</char> vineyard, <char style="add">[and]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> oliveyard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Six days you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do you<char style="ord">i</char> work, and on the seventh day you<char style="ord">i</char> shall rest: that you<char style="ord">i</char> ox and you<char style="ord">i</char> ass may rest, and the son of you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, and the stranger, may be refreshed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And in all <char style="add">[things]</char> that I have said unto you be circumspect <char style="pn">(be watchful every way; take heed)</char>: and make no mention of the name of other gods, neither let it be heard out of you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Three times you<char style="ord">i</char> shall keep a feast unto me in the year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall keep the feast of unleavened bread: <char style="pn">(you <char style="ord">i</char> shall eat unleavened bread seven days, as I commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>, in the time appointed of the month Aviv; for in it you<char style="ord">i</char> came out from Mitzrayim [Egypt - The Narrow Place]: and none shall appear before me empty:)</char></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the feast of harvest, the first fruits of you<char style="ord">i</char> labours, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have sown in the field: and the feast of ingathering, <char style="add">[which is]</char> in the end of the year, when you<char style="ord">i</char> have gathered in you<char style="ord">i</char> labours out of the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Three times in the year all you<char style="ord">i</char> males shall appear before the Lord-Adon <char style="add">[Ruler of the Earth]</char> God-Yehovah <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leavened bread; neither shall the fat of my sacrifice remain until the morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />The first of the first fruits of you<char style="ord">i</char> land you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not seethe a kid in his mother’s milk.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Behold, I send an Angel before you<char style="ord">i</char>, to keep you<char style="ord">i</char> in the way, and to bring you<char style="ord">i</char> into the place which I have prepared.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Beware of him, and obey his voice, provoke him not; for he will not pardon your transgressions: for my name <char style="add">[is]</char> in him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">i</char> shall indeed obey his voice, and do all that I speak; then I will be an enemy unto you<char style="ord">i</char> enemies, and an adversary unto you<char style="ord">i</char> adversaries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For my Angel shall go before you<char style="ord">i</char>, and bring you<char style="ord">i</char> in unto the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>, and the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, the Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>: and I will cut them off.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not bow down to their gods, nor serve them, nor do after their works: but you<char style="ord">i</char> shall utterly overthrow them, and quite break down their images.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and he shall bless you<char style="ord">i</char> bread, and you<char style="ord">i</char> water; and I will take sickness away from the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />There shall nothing cast their young, nor be barren, in you<char style="ord">i</char> land: the number of you<char style="ord">i</char> days I will fulfill.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />I will send my fear before you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will destroy all the people to whom you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come, and I will make all you<char style="ord">i</char> enemies turn their backs unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And I will send hornets before you<char style="ord">i</char>, which shall drive out the Hivi <char style="add">[Wicked Villagers]</char>, the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchants]</char>, and the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, from before you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />I will not drive them out from before you<char style="ord">i</char> in one year; lest the land become desolate, and the beast of the field multiply against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />By little and little I will drive them out from before you<char style="ord">i</char>, until you<char style="ord">i</char> be increased, and inherit the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And I will set you<char style="ord">i</char> bounds from the Red sea even unto the sea of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and from the desert unto the river: for I will deliver the inhabitants of the land into your hand; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall drive them out before you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make no covenant with them, nor with their gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />They shall not dwell in you<char style="ord">i</char> land, lest they make you<char style="ord">i</char> sin against me: for if you<char style="ord">i</char> serve their gods, it will surely be a snare unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And he said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Come up unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char>, and Avihu <char style="add">[he is my father]</char>, and seventy of the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and worship you<char style="ord">2f</char> afar off.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> alone shall come near the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: but they shall not come near; neither shall the people go up with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> came and told the people all the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and all the judgments: and all the people answered with one voice, and said, All the words which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has said will we do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> wrote all the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and rose up early in the morning, and built an altar under the hill, and twelve pillars, according to the twelve tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he sent young men of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which offered burnt offerings, and sacrificed peace offerings of oxen unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> took half of the blood, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> in basins; and half of the blood he sprinkled on the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he took the book of the covenant, and read in the audience of the people: and they said, All that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has said will we do, and be obedient.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> took the blood, and sprinkled <char style="add">[it]</char> on the people, and said, Behold the blood of the covenant, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has made with you concerning all these words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then went up Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char>, and Avihu <char style="add">[he is my father]</char>, and seventy of the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they saw the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and <char style="add">[there was]</char> under his feet as it were a paved work of a sapphire stone, and as it were the body of heaven in <char style="add">[his]</char> clearness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And upon the nobles of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> he laid not his hand: also they saw God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and did eat and drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Come up to me into the mount, and be there: and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> tables of stone, and a law, and commandments which I have written; that you<char style="ord">i</char> may teach them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> rose up, and his minister Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went up into the mount of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said unto the elders, Tarry you<char style="ord">2f</char> here for us, until we come again unto you: and, behold, Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and Hur <char style="add">[Liberty] [are]</char> with you: if any man have any matters to do, let him come unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went up into the mount, and a cloud covered the mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> abode upon mount Sinai, and the cloud covered it six days: and the seventh day he called unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> out of the midst of the cloud.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the sight of the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> like devouring fire on the top of the mount in the eyes of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went into the midst of the cloud, and got him up into the mount: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> was in the mount forty days and forty nights.</para>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Speak unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that they bring me an offering: of every man that gives it willingly with his heart you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall take my offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[is]</char> the offering which you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall take of them; gold, and silver, and brass,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And rams’ skins dyed red, and badgers’ skins, and shittim wood,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Oil for the light, spices for anointing oil, and for sweet incense,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Onyx stones, and stones to be set in the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and in the breastplate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And let them make me a sanctuary; that I may dwell among them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />According to all that I show you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[after]</char> the pattern of the tabernacle, and the pattern of all the instruments thereof, even so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> make <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they shall make an ark <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood: two cubits and a half <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the length thereof, and a cubit and a half the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall overlay it with pure gold, within and without shall you<char style="ord">i</char> overlay it, and shall make upon it a crown of gold round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall cast four rings of gold for it, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> in the four corners thereof; and two rings <char style="add">[shall be]</char> in the one side of it, and two rings in the other side of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlay them with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> into the rings by the sides of the ark, that the ark may be borne with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> shall be in the rings of the ark: they shall not be taken from it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put into the ark the testimony which I shall give you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make a mercy seat <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold: two cubits and a half <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the length thereof, and a cubit and a half the breadth thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make two cherubim <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, <char style="add">[of]</char> beaten work shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make them, in the two ends of the mercy seat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And make one cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> on the one end, and the other cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> on the other end: <char style="add">[even]</char> of the mercy seat shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> make the cherubim on the two ends thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the cherubim shall stretch forth <char style="add">[their]</char> wings on high, covering the mercy seat with their wings, and their faces <char style="add">[shall look]</char> one to another; toward the mercy seat shall the faces of the cherubim be.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the mercy seat above upon the ark; and in the ark you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the testimony that I shall give you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And there I will meet with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will commune with you<char style="ord">i</char> from above the mercy seat, from between the two cherubim which <char style="add">[are]</char> upon the ark of the testimony, of all <char style="add">[things]</char> which I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> in commandment unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall also make a table <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood: two cubits <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall overlay it with pure gold, and make thereto a crown of gold round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make unto it a border of an hand breadth round about, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make a golden crown to the border thereof round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make for it four rings of gold, and put the rings in the four corners that <char style="add">[are]</char> on the four feet thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Over against the border shall the rings be for places of the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> to bear the table.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlay them with gold, that the table may be borne with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the dishes thereof, and spoons thereof, and covers thereof, and bowls thereof, to cover withal: <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set upon the table showbread before me always.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make a candlestick <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold: <char style="add">[of]</char> beaten work shall the candlestick be made: his shaft, and his branches, his bowls, his knops, and his flowers, shall be of the same.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And six branches shall come out of the sides of it; three branches of the candlestick out of the one side, and three branches of the candlestick out of the other side:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Three bowls made like unto almonds, <char style="add">[with]</char> a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> and a flower in one branch; and three bowls made like almonds in the other branch, <char style="add">[with]</char> a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> and a flower: so in the six branches that come out of the candlestick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And in the candlestick <char style="add">[shall be]</char> four bowls made like unto almonds, <char style="add">[with]</char> their knops and their flowers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> under two branches of the same, and a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> under two branches of the same, and a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> under two branches of the same, according to the six branches that proceed out of the candlestick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Their knops and their branches shall be of the same: all it <char style="add">[shall be]</char> one beaten work <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the seven lamps thereof: and they shall light the lamps thereof, that they may give light over against it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the tongs thereof, and the snuff dishes thereof, <char style="add">[shall be of]</char> pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Of]</char> a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> of pure gold shall he make it, with all these vessels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And look that you<char style="ord">i</char> make <char style="add">[them]</char> after their pattern, which was showed you<char style="ord">i</char> in the mount.</para>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the tabernacle <char style="add">[with]</char> ten curtains <char style="add">[of]</char> fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet: <char style="add">[with]</char> cherubim of cunning work shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The length of one curtain <char style="add">[shall be]</char> eight and twenty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and every one of the curtains shall have one measure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The five curtains shall be coupled together one to another; and <char style="add">[other]</char> five curtains <char style="add">[shall be]</char> coupled one to another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make loops of blue upon the edge of the one curtain from the selvedge <char style="pn">(fabric edge to prevent unraveling)</char> in the coupling; and likewise shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make in the uttermost edge of <char style="add">[another]</char> curtain, in the coupling of the second.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Fifty loops shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make in the one curtain, and fifty loops shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make in the edge of the curtain that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the coupling of the second; that the loops may take hold one of another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make fifty hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char> of gold, and couple the curtains together with the hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char>: and it shall be one tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make curtains <char style="add">[of]</char> goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char> to be a covering upon the tabernacle: eleven curtains shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The length of one curtain <char style="add">[shall be]</char> thirty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and the eleven curtains <char style="add">[shall be all]</char> of one measure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall couple five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves, and shall double the sixth curtain in the forefront of the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make fifty loops on the edge of the one curtain <char style="add">[that is]</char> outmost in the coupling, and fifty loops in the edge of the curtain which couples the second.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make fifty hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char> of brass, and put the hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char> into the loops, and couple the tent together, that it may be one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the remnant that remains of the curtains of the tent, the half curtain that remains, shall hang over the backside of the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And a cubit on the one side, and a cubit on the other side of that which remains in the length of the curtains of the tent, it shall hang over the sides of the tabernacle on this side and on that side, to cover it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make a covering for the tent <char style="add">[of]</char> rams’ skins dyed red, and a covering above <char style="add">[of]</char> badgers’ skins.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make boards for the tabernacle <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood standing up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Ten cubits <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the length of a board, and a cubit and a half <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the breadth of one board.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Two tenons <char style="add">[shall there be]</char> in one board, set in order one against another: thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make for all the boards of the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the boards for the tabernacle, twenty boards on the south side southward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for his two tenons, and two sockets under another board for his two tenons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And for the second side of the tabernacle on the north side <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> twenty boards:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And their forty sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> silver; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And for the sides of the tabernacle westward you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make six boards.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And two boards shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make for the corners of the tabernacle in the two sides.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And they shall be coupled together beneath, and they shall be coupled together above the head of it unto one ring: thus shall it be for them both; they shall be for the two corners.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they shall be eight boards, and their sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> silver, sixteen sockets; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make bars <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood; five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the side of the tabernacle, for the two sides westward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the middle bar in the midst of the boards shall reach from end to end.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall overlay the boards with gold, and make their rings <char style="add">[of]</char> gold <char style="add">[for]</char> places for the bars: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall overlay the bars with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall rear up the tabernacle according to the fashion thereof which was showed you<char style="ord">i</char> in the mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make a veil <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen of cunning work: with cherubim shall it be made:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall hang it upon four pillars of shittim <char style="add">[wood]</char> overlaid with gold: their hooks <char style="add">[shall be of]</char> gold, upon the four sockets of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall hang up the veil under the hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may bring in there within the veil the ark of the testimony: and the veil shall divide unto you between the holy <char style="add">[place]</char> and the most holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the mercy seat upon the ark of the testimony in the most holy <char style="add">[place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set the table without the veil, and the candlestick over against the table on the side of the tabernacle toward the south: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the table on the north side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make an hanging for the door of the tent, <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, wrought with needlework.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make for the hanging five pillars <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim <char style="add">[wood]</char>, and overlay them with gold, <char style="add">[and]</char> their hooks <char style="add">[shall be of]</char> gold: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall cast five sockets of brass for them.</para>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make an altar <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, five cubits long, and five cubits broad; the altar shall be Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char>: and the height thereof <char style="add">[shall be]</char> three cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the horns of it upon the four corners thereof: his horns shall be of the same: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall overlay it with brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make his pans to receive his ashes, and his shovels, and his basins, and his flesh hooks, and his fire pans: all the vessels thereof you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make <char style="add">[of]</char> brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make for it a grate of network <char style="add">[of]</char> brass; and upon the net shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make four brazen rings in the four corners thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put it under the compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> of the altar beneath, that the net may be even to the midst of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> for the altar, rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlay them with brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> shall be put into the rings, and the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> shall be upon the two sides of the altar, to bear it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Hollow with boards shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make it: as it was showed you<char style="ord">i</char> in the mount, so shall they make <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the court of the tabernacle: for the south side southward <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> hangings for the court <char style="add">[of]</char> fine twined linen of an hundred cubits long for one side:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the twenty pillars thereof and their twenty sockets <char style="add">[shall be of]</char> brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets <char style="add">[shall be of]</char> silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And likewise for the north side in length <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> hangings of an hundred <char style="add">[cubits]</char> long, and his twenty pillars and their twenty sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets <char style="add">[of]</char> silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And <char style="add">[for]</char> the breadth of the court on the west side <char style="add">[shall be]</char> hangings of fifty cubits: their pillars ten, and their sockets ten.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the breadth of the court on the east side eastward <char style="add">[shall be]</char> fifty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The hangings of one side <char style="add">[of the gate shall be]</char> fifteen cubits: their pillars three, and their sockets three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And on the other side <char style="add">[shall be]</char> hangings fifteen <char style="add">[cubits]</char>: their pillars three, and their sockets three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And for the gate of the court <char style="add">[shall be]</char> an hanging of twenty cubits, <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, wrought with needlework: <char style="add">[and]</char> their pillars <char style="add">[shall be]</char> four, and their sockets four.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />All the pillars round about the court <char style="add">[shall be]</char> filleted with silver; their hooks <char style="add">[shall be of]</char> silver, and their sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The length of the court <char style="add">[shall be]</char> an hundred cubits, and the breadth fifty everywhere, and the height five cubits <char style="add">[of]</char> fine twined linen, and their sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />All the vessels of the tabernacle in all the service thereof, and all the pins thereof, and all the pins of the court, <char style="add">[shall be of]</char> brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall command the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that they bring you<char style="ord">i</char> pure oil olive beaten for the light, to cause the lamp to burn always.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />In the tabernacle of the congregation without the veil, which <char style="add">[is]</char> before the testimony, Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons shall order it from evening to morning before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: <char style="add">[it shall be]</char> a statute forever unto their generations on the behalf of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And take you<char style="ord">i</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char> Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother, and his sons with him, from among the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office, <char style="add">[even]</char> Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char> and Avihu <char style="add">[he is my father]</char>, El’azar <char style="add">[God has helped]</char> and Itamar <char style="add">[Coast of Palms]</char>, Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make holy garments for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother for glory and for beauty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak unto all <char style="add">[that are]</char> wise hearted, whom I have filled with the spirit of wisdom, that they may make Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s garments to consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> him, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> the garments which they shall make; a breastplate, and an ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and a robe, and a adorned with needlework coat, a mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char>, and a belt: and they shall make holy garments for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother, and his sons, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they shall take gold, and blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they shall make the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and <char style="add">[of]</char> purple, <char style="add">[of]</char> scarlet, and fine twined linen, with cunning work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />It shall have the two shoulder pieces thereof joined at the two edges thereof; and <char style="add">[so]</char> it shall be joined together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> belt of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> upon it, shall be of the same, according to the work thereof; <char style="add">[even of]</char> gold, <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take two onyx stones, and grave on them the names of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Six of their names on one stone, and <char style="add">[the other]</char> six names of the rest on the other stone, according to their birth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />With the work of an engraver in stone, <char style="add">[like]</char> the engravings of a signet <char style="pn">(seal or stamp)</char>, shall you<char style="ord">i</char> engrave the two stones with the names of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make them to be set in sockets of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the two stones upon the shoulders of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> <char style="add">[for]</char> stones of memorial unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> shall bear their names before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> upon his two shoulders for a memorial.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> gold;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And two chains <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold at the ends; <char style="add">[of]</char> wreathen work shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make them, and fasten the wreathen chains to the sockets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the breastplate of judgment with cunning work; after the work of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make it; <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and <char style="add">[of]</char> purple, and <char style="add">[of]</char> scarlet, and <char style="add">[of]</char> fine twined linen, shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char> it shall be <char style="add">[being]</char> doubled; a span <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the length thereof, and a span <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the breadth thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set in it settings of stones, <char style="add">[even]</char> four rows of stones: <char style="add">[the first]</char> row <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a sardius, a topaz, and a Carbuncle <char style="pn">(a red precious stone)</char>: <char style="add">[this shall be]</char> the first row.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the second row <char style="add">[shall be]</char> an emerald, a sapphire, and a diamond.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the third row a ligure, an agate, and an amethyst.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the fourth row a beryl, and an onyx, and a jasper: they shall be set in gold in their inclosings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the stones shall be with the names of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, twelve, according to their names, <char style="add">[like]</char> the engravings of a signet <char style="pn">(seal or stamp)</char>; every one with his name shall they be according to the twelve tribes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make upon the breastplate chains at the ends <char style="add">[of]</char> wreathen work <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make upon the breastplate two rings of gold, and shall put the two rings on the two ends of the breastplate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the two wreathen <char style="add">[chains]</char> of gold in the two rings <char style="add">[which are]</char> on the ends of the breastplate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And <char style="add">[the other]</char> two ends of the two wreathen <char style="add">[chains]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall fasten in the two sockets, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> on the shoulder pieces of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> before it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make two rings of gold, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put them upon the two ends of the breastplate in the border thereof, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the side of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> inward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And two <char style="add">[other]</char> rings of gold you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make, and shall put them on the two sides of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> underneath, toward the forepart thereof, over against the <char style="add">[other]</char> coupling thereof, above the detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> belt of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And they shall bind the breastplate by the rings thereof unto the rings of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> with a lace of blue, that <char style="add">[it]</char> may be above the detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> belt of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and that the breastplate be not loosed from the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> shall bear the names of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in the breastplate of judgment upon his heart, when he goes in unto the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>, for a memorial before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> continually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put in the breastplate of judgment the Urim <char style="add">[Lights]</char> and the Tumim <char style="add">[Perfection]</char>; and they shall be upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s heart, when he goes in before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> shall bear the judgment of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> upon his heart before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> continually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the robe of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> all <char style="add">[of]</char> blue.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And there shall be an hole in the top of it, in the midst thereof: it shall have a binding of woven work round about the hole of it, as it were the hole of an habergeon <char style="pn">(coat of mail for the neck and down)</char>, that it be not rent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And <char style="add">[beneath]</char> upon the hem of it you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make pomegranates <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and <char style="add">[of]</char> purple, and <char style="add">[of]</char> scarlet, round about the hem thereof; and bells of gold between them round about:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />A golden bell and a pomegranate, a golden bell and a pomegranate, upon the hem of the robe round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And it shall be upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> to minister: and his sound shall be heard when he goes in unto the holy <char style="add">[place]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and when he comes out, that he die not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make a plate <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold, and grave upon it, <char style="add">[like]</char> the engravings of a signet <char style="pn">(seal or stamp)</char>, HOLINESS TO THE LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put it on a blue lace, that it may be upon the mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char>; upon the forefront of the mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char> it shall be.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And it shall be upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s forehead, that Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> may bear the iniquity of the holy things, which the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall hallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> in all their holy gifts; and it shall be always upon his forehead, that they may be accepted before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall embroider the coat of fine linen, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> fine linen, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the belt <char style="add">[of]</char> needlework.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s sons you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make coats, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make for them girdles, and bonnets shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make for them, for glory and for beauty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put them upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother, and his sons with him; and shall anoint them, and consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> them, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> them, that they may minister unto me in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make them linen trousers to cover their nakedness; from the waist even unto the thighs they shall reach:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And they shall be upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and upon his sons, when they come in unto the tabernacle of the congregation, or when they come near unto the altar to minister in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>; that they bear not iniquity, and die: <char style="add">[it shall be]</char> a statute forever unto him and his seed after him.</para>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do unto them to hallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> them, to minister unto me in the priest’s office: Take one young bullock, and two rams without blemish,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And unleavened bread, and cakes unleavened tempered with oil, and wafers unleavened anointed with oil: <char style="add">[of]</char> wheaten flour shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put them into one basket, and bring them in the basket, with the bullock and the two rams.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall wash them with water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take the garments, and put upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the coat, and the robe of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and the breastplate, and gird him with the detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> belt of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put the mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char> upon his head, and put the holy crown upon the mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then shall you<char style="ord">i</char> take the anointing oil, and pour <char style="add">[it]</char> upon his head, and anoint him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring his sons, and put coats upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall gird them with girdles, Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons, and put the bonnets on them: and the priest’s office shall be theirs for a perpetual statute: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall cause a bullock to be brought before the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons shall put their hands upon the head of the bullock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall kill the bullock before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[by]</char> the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take of the blood of the bullock, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> upon the horns of the altar with you<char style="ord">i</char> finger, and pour all the blood beside the bottom of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take all the fat that covers the inwards, and the caul <char style="pn">(membrane; fatty tissue around a bodily organ)</char> <char style="add">[that is]</char> above the liver, and the two kidneys, and the fat that <char style="add">[is]</char> upon them, and burn <char style="add">[them]</char> upon the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But the flesh of the bullock, and his skin, and his dung, shall you<char style="ord">i</char> burn with fire without the camp: it <char style="add">[is]</char> a sin offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall also take one ram; and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons shall put their hands upon the head of the ram.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall slay the ram, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take his blood, and sprinkle <char style="add">[it]</char> round about upon the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall cut the ram in pieces, and wash the inwards of him, and his legs, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> unto his pieces, and unto his head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall burn the whole ram upon the altar: it <char style="add">[is]</char> a burnt offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: it <char style="add">[is]</char> a soothing aroma, an offering made by fire unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take the other ram; and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons shall put their hands upon the head of the ram.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then shall you<char style="ord">i</char> kill the ram, and take of his blood, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> upon the tip of the right ear of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and upon the tip of the right ear of his sons, and upon the thumb of their right hand, and upon the great toe of their right foot, and sprinkle the blood upon the altar round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take of the blood that <char style="add">[is]</char> upon the altar, and of the anointing oil, and sprinkle <char style="add">[it]</char> upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and upon his garments, and upon his sons, and upon the garments of his sons with him: and he shall be consecrated, and his garments, and his sons, and his sons’ garments with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Also you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take of the ram the fat and the rump, and the fat that covers the inwards, and the caul <char style="pn">(membrane; fatty tissue around a bodily organ)</char> <char style="add">[above]</char> the liver, and the two kidneys, and the fat that <char style="add">[is]</char> upon them, and the right shoulder; for it <char style="add">[is]</char> a ram of consecration:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And one loaf of bread, and one cake of oiled bread, and one wafer out of the basket of the unleavened bread that <char style="add">[is]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put all in the hands of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and in the hands of his sons; and shall wave them <char style="add">[for]</char> a wave offering before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall receive them of their hands, and burn <char style="add">[them]</char> upon the altar for a burnt offering, for a soothing aroma before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: it <char style="add">[is]</char> an offering made by fire unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take the breast of the ram of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s consecration, and wave it <char style="add">[for]</char> a wave offering before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and it shall be you<char style="ord">i</char> part.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> the breast of the wave offering, and the shoulder of the heave offering, which is waved, and which is heaved up, of the ram of the consecration, <char style="add">[even]</char> of <char style="add">[that]</char> which <char style="add">[is]</char> for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and of <char style="add">[that]</char> which is for his sons:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And it shall be Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>’s and his sons’ by a statute forever from the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for it <char style="add">[is]</char> an heave offering: and it shall be an heave offering from the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> of the sacrifice of their peace offerings, <char style="add">[even]</char> their heave offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the holy garments of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> shall be his sons’ after him, to be anointed in it, and to be consecrated in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> that son that is priest in his stead shall put them on seven days, when he comes into the tabernacle of the congregation to minister in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take the ram of the consecration, and seethe his flesh in the holy place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons shall eat the flesh of the ram, and the bread that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the basket, <char style="add">[by]</char> the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And they shall eat those things which the atonement was made, to consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> <char style="add">[and]</char> to sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> them: but a stranger shall not eat <char style="add">[thereof]</char>, because they <char style="add">[are]</char> holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And if ought of the flesh of the consecrations, or of the bread, remain unto the morning, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall burn the remainder with fire: it shall not be eaten, because it <char style="add">[is]</char> holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> do unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and to his sons, according to all <char style="add">[things]</char> which I have commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>: seven days shall you<char style="ord">i</char> consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer every day a bullock <char style="add">[for]</char> a sin offering for atonement: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall cleanse the altar, when you<char style="ord">i</char> have made an atonement for it, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint it, to sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Seven days you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make an atonement for the altar, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> it; and it shall be an altar most holy: whatsoever touches the altar shall be holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />Now this <char style="add">[is that]</char> which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer upon the altar; two lambs of the first year day by day continually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />The one lamb you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer in the morning; and the other lamb you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer at even:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And with the one lamb a tenth deal of flour mingled with the fourth part of an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char> of beaten oil; and the fourth part of an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char> of wine <char style="add">[for]</char> a drink offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And the other lamb you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer at even, and shall do thereto according to the meat offering of the morning, and according to the drink offering thereof, for a soothing aroma, an offering made by fire unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[This shall be]</char> a continual burnt offering throughout your generations <char style="add">[at]</char> the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: where I will meet you, to speak there unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And there I will meet with the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and <char style="add">[the tabernacle]</char> shall be sanctified by my glory.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And I will sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> the tabernacle of the congregation, and the altar: I will sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> also both Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons, to minister to me in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And I will dwell among the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and will be their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />And they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that brought them forth out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, that I may dwell among them: I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make an altar to burn incense upon: <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />A cubit <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof; Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char> shall it be: and two cubits <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the height thereof: the horns thereof <char style="add">[shall be]</char> of the same.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall overlay it with pure gold, the top thereof, and the sides thereof round about, and the horns thereof; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make unto it a crown of gold round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And two golden rings shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make to it under the crown of it, by the two corners thereof, upon the two sides of it shall you<char style="ord">i</char> make <char style="add">[it]</char>; and they shall be for places for the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> to bear it withal.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlay them with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put it before the veil that <char style="add">[is]</char> by the ark of the testimony, before the mercy seat that <char style="add">[is]</char> over the testimony, where I will meet with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> shall burn thereon sweet incense every morning: when he dresses the lamps, he shall burn incense upon it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And when Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> lights the lamps at even, he shall burn incense upon it, a perpetual incense before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> throughout your generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall offer no strange incense thereon, nor burnt sacrifice, nor meat offering; neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> pour drink offering thereon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> shall make an atonement upon the horns of it once in a year with the blood of the sin offering of atonements: once in the year shall he make atonement upon it throughout your generations: it <char style="add">[is]</char> most holy unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />When you<char style="ord">i</char> take the sum of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> after their number, then shall they give every man a ransom for his soul unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when you<char style="ord">i</char> them; that there be no plague among them, when <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> numbers them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />This they shall give, every one that passes among them that are numbered, half a shekel after the shekel of the sanctuary <char style="pn">(a shekel [is] twenty gerahs:) an half shekel [shall be] the offering of the LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Khav’vah <char style="add">[Eve]</char> <char style="pn">(to breath, to live)</char> every one that passes among them that are numbered, from twenty years old and above, shall give an offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The rich shall not give more, and the poor shall not give less than half a shekel, when <char style="add">[they]</char> give an offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to make an atonement for your souls.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take the atonement money of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and shall appoint it for the service of the tabernacle of the congregation; that it may be a memorial unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to make an atonement for your souls.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall also make a Wash basin <char style="add">[of]</char> brass, and his foot <char style="add">[also of]</char> brass, to wash <char style="add">[withal]</char>: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put it between the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put water in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons shall wash their hands and their feet thereat:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />When they go into the tabernacle of the congregation, they shall wash with water, that they die not; or when they come near to the altar to minister, to burn offering made by fire unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So they shall wash their hands and their feet, that they die not: and it shall be a statute forever to them, <char style="add">[even]</char> to him and to his seed throughout their generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Moreover the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Take you<char style="ord">i</char> also unto you<char style="ord">i</char> principal spices, of pure myrrh five hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char>, and of sweet cinnamon half so much, <char style="add">[even]</char> two hundred and fifty <char style="add">[shekels]</char>, and of sweet calamus two hundred and fifty <char style="add">[shekels]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And of cassia five hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char>, after the shekel of the sanctuary, and of oil olive an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make it an oil of holy ointment, an ointment compound after the are of the apothecary: it shall be an holy anointing oil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint the tabernacle of the congregation with that, and the ark of the testimony,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the table and all his vessels, and the candlestick and his vessels, and the altar of incense,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the altar of burnt offering with all his vessels, and the Wash basin and his foot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> them, that they may be most holy: whatsoever touches them shall be holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons, and consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> them, that <char style="add">[they]</char> may minister unto me in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, This shall be an holy anointing oil unto me throughout your generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Upon man’s flesh shall it not be poured, neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> make <char style="add">[any other]</char> like it, after the composition of it: it <char style="add">[is]</char> holy, <char style="add">[and]</char> it shall be holy unto you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Whosoever compounds <char style="add">[any]</char> like it, or whosoever puts <char style="add">[any]</char> of it upon a stranger, shall even be cut off from his people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Take unto you<char style="ord">i</char> sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; <char style="add">[these]</char> sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like <char style="add">[weight]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make it a perfume, a confection after the are of the apothecary, tempered together, pure <char style="add">[and]</char> holy:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall beat <char style="add">[some]</char> of it very small, and put of it before the testimony in the tabernacle of the congregation, where I will meet with you<char style="ord">i</char>: it shall be unto you most holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as for]</char> the perfume which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not make to yourselves according to the composition thereof: it shall be unto you<char style="ord">i</char> holy for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />Whosoever shall make like unto that, to smell thereto, shall even be cut off from his people.</para>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />See, I have called by name B’tzal’el <char style="add">[In The Shadow (Protection) of El / God]</char> the son of Uri <char style="add">[my light, my fire]</char>, the son of Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char>, of the tribe of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I have filled him with the spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />To devise cunning works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And in cutting of stones, to set <char style="add">[them]</char>, and in carving of timber, to work in all manner of workmanship.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I, behold, I have given with him Oholi’av <char style="add">[Father’s Tent]</char>, the son of Achisamakh <char style="add">[My Brother is Strength]</char>, of the tribe of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>: and in the hearts of all that are wise hearted I have put wisdom, that they may make all that I have commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />The tabernacle of the congregation, and the ark of the testimony, and the mercy seat that <char style="add">[is]</char> thereupon, and all the furniture of the tabernacle,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the table and his furniture, and the pure candlestick with all his furniture, and the altar of incense,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the altar of burnt offering with all his furniture, and the Wash basin and his foot,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the cloths of service, and the holy garments for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest’s office,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the anointing oil, and sweet incense for the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>: according to all that I have commanded you<char style="ord">i</char> shall they do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Speak you<char style="ord">i</char> also unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Truly my Shabbat you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall keep: for it <char style="add">[is]</char> a sign between me and you throughout your generations; that <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">2f</char>]</char> may know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that does sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall keep the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> therefore; for it <char style="add">[is]</char> holy unto you: every one that defiles it shall surely be put to death: for whosoever does <char style="add">[any]</char> work in it, that soul shall be cut off from among his people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Six days may work be done; but in the seventh <char style="add">[is]</char> the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> of rest, holy to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: whosoever does <char style="add">[any]</char> work in the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day, he shall surely be put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For what reason the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall keep the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, to observe the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> throughout their generations, <char style="add">[for]</char> a perpetual covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />It <char style="add">[is]</char> a sign between me and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> forever: for <char style="add">[in]</char> six days the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> made heaven and earth, and on the seventh day he rested, and was refreshed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he gave unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, when he had made an end of communing with him upon mount Sinai, two tables of testimony, tables of stone, written with the finger of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="32" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And when the people saw that Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> delayed to come down out of the mount, the people gathered themselves together unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and said unto him, Up, make us gods, which shall go before us; for <char style="add">[as for]</char> this Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, the man that brought us up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, we know not what is become of him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> said unto them, Break off the golden earrings, which <char style="add">[are]</char> in the ears of your wives, of your sons, and of your daughters, and bring <char style="add">[them]</char> unto me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And all the people broke off the golden earrings which <char style="add">[were]</char> in their ears, and brought <char style="add">[them]</char> unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he received <char style="add">[them]</char> at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, after he had made it a molten calf: and they said, These <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> gods, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which brought you<char style="ord">i</char> up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, he built an altar before it; and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> made proclamation, and said, Tomorrow <char style="add">[is]</char> a feast to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they rose up early on the morrow, and offered burnt offerings, and brought peace offerings; and the people sat down to eat and to drink, and rose up to play.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Go, get you<char style="ord">i</char> down; for you<char style="ord">i</char> people, which you<char style="ord">i</char> brought out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, have corrupted <char style="add">[themselves]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />They have turned aside quickly out of the way which I commanded them: they have made them a molten calf, and have worshipped it, and have sacrificed thereunto, and said, These <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> gods, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which have brought you<char style="ord">i</char> up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, I have seen this people, and, behold, it <char style="add">[is]</char> a stiff-necked people:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Now therefore let me alone, that my wrath may grow <char style="pn">(become; advance)</char> hot against them, and that I may consume them: and I will make of you<char style="ord">i</char> a great nation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> besought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and said, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, why does you<char style="ord">i</char> wrath grow <char style="pn">(become; advance)</char> hot against you<char style="ord">i</char> people, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought forth out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> with great power, and with a mighty hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />For what reason should the Mitzri speak, and say, For mischief did he bring them out, to slay them in the mountains, and to consume them from the face of the earth? Turn from you<char style="ord">i</char> fierce wrath, and repent of this evil against you<char style="ord">i</char> people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Remember Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, to whom you<char style="ord">i</char> swore by your<char style="ord">i</char> own self, and said unto them, I will multiply your seed as the stars of heaven, and all this land that I have spoken of will I give unto your seed, and they shall inherit <char style="add">[it]</char> forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> repented of the evil which he thought to do unto his people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> turned, and went down from the mount, and the two tables of the testimony <char style="add">[were]</char> in his hand: the tables <char style="add">[were]</char> written on both their sides; on the one side and on the other <char style="add">[were]</char> they written.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the tables <char style="add">[were]</char> the work of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and the writing <char style="add">[was]</char> the writing of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, graven upon the tables.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And when Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> heard the noise of the people as they shouted, he said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, <char style="add">[There is]</char> a noise of war in the camp.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said, <char style="add">[It is]</char> not the voice of <char style="add">[them that]</char> shout for mastery, neither <char style="add">[is it]</char> the voice of <char style="add">[them that]</char> cry for being overcome: <char style="add">[but]</char> the noise of <char style="add">[them that]</char> sing do I hear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And it came to pass, as soon as he came near unto the camp, that he saw the calf, and the dancing: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ anger waxed hot, and he cast the tables out of his hands, and broke them beneath the mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he took the calf which they had made, and burnt <char style="add">[it]</char> in the fire, and ground <char style="add">[it]</char> to powder, and scattered <char style="add">[it]</char> upon the water, and made the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> drink <char style="add">[of it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, What did this people unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought so great a sin upon them?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> said, Let not the anger of my lord grow <char style="pn">(become; advance)</char> hot: you<char style="ord">i</char> know the people, that they <char style="add">[are set]</char> on mischief.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For they said unto me, Make us gods, which shall go before us: for <char style="add">[as for]</char> this Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, the man that brought us up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, we know not what is become of him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And I said unto them, Whosoever has any gold, let them break <char style="add">[it]</char> off. So they gave <char style="add">[it]</char> me: then I cast it into the fire, and there came out this calf.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And when Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> saw that the people <char style="add">[were]</char> naked; <char style="pn">(for Aharon [Bright, Very High] had made them naked unto [their] shame among their enemies:)</char></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Then Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> stood in the gate of the camp, and said, Who <char style="add">[is]</char> on the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> side? <char style="add">[let him come]</char> unto me. And all the sons of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char> gathered themselves together unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he said unto them, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Put every man his sword by his side, <char style="add">[and]</char> go in and out from gate to gate throughout the camp, and slay every man his brother, and every man his companion, and every man his neighbour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the children of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char> did according to the word of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>: and there fell of the people that day about three thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />For Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> had said, Consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> yourselves today to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, even every man upon his son, and upon his brother; that he may bestow upon you a blessing this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, that Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the people, You<char style="ord">2f</char> have sinned a great sin: and now I will go up unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; perhaps I shall make an atonement for your sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> returned unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, Oh, this people have sinned a great sin, and have made them gods of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Yet now, if you<char style="ord">i</char> will forgive their sin--; and if not, blot me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, out of you<char style="ord">i</char> book which you<char style="ord">i</char> have written.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Whosoever has sinned against me, him will I blot out of my book.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Therefore now go, lead the people unto <char style="add">[the place]</char> of which I have spoken unto you<char style="ord">i</char>: behold, my Angel shall go before you<char style="ord">i</char>: nevertheless in the day when I visit I will visit their sin upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> plagued the people, because they made the calf, which Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> made.</para>
  <chapter number="33" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Depart, <char style="add">[and]</char> go up hence, you<char style="ord">i</char> and the people which you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, unto the land which I swear unto Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, to Yitz’chak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and to Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, saying, Unto you<char style="ord">i</char> seed will I give it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And I will send an angel before you<char style="ord">i</char>; and I will drive out the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchants]</char>, the Emori <char style="add">[Rebellious Highlanders]</char>, and the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, the Hivi <char style="add">[Wicked Villagers]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Unto a land flowing with milk and honey: for I will not go up in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>; for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a stiff-necked people: lest I consume you<char style="ord">i</char> in the way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And when the people heard these evil tidings, they mourned: and no man did put on him his ornaments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Say unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a stiff-necked people: I will come up into the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char> in a moment, and consume you<char style="ord">i</char>: therefore now put off you<char style="ord">i</char> ornaments from you<char style="ord">i</char>, that I may know what to do unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> stripped themselves of their ornaments by the mount Horev <char style="add">[Desert]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> took the tabernacle, and pitched it without the camp, afar off from the camp, and called it the Tabernacle of the congregation. And it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> every one which sought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> went out unto the tabernacle of the congregation, which <char style="add">[was]</char> without the camp.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went out unto the tabernacle, <char style="add">[that]</char> all the people rose up, and stood every man <char style="add">[at]</char> his tent door, and looked after Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, until he was gone into the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it came to pass, as Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> entered into the tabernacle, the cloudy pillar descended, and stood <char style="add">[at]</char> the door of the tabernacle, and <char style="add">[the LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)]</char> talked with Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And all the people saw the cloudy pillar stand <char style="add">[at]</char> the tabernacle door: and all the people rose up and worshipped, every man <char style="add">[in]</char> his tent door.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> face to face, as a man speaks unto his friend. And he turned again into the camp: but his servant Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, the son of Nun <char style="add">[Posterity]</char>, a young man, departed not out of the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, See, you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto me, Bring up this people: and you<char style="ord">i</char> have not let me know whom you<char style="ord">i</char> will send with me. Yet you<char style="ord">i</char> have said, I know you<char style="ord">i</char> by name, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have also found grace in my sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, if I have found grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> sight, show me now you<char style="ord">i</char> way, that I may know you<char style="ord">i</char>, that I may find grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> sight: and consider that this nation <char style="add">[is]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said, My presence shall go [with you<char style="ord">i</char>], and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> rest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said unto him, If you<char style="ord">i</char> presence go not <char style="add">[with me]</char>, carry us not up hence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For wherein shall it be known here that I and you<char style="ord">i</char> people have found grace in your<char style="ord">i</char> sight? <char style="add">[is it]</char> not in that you<char style="ord">i</char> go with us? so shall we be separated, I and you<char style="ord">i</char> people, from all the people that <char style="add">[are]</char> upon the face of the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, I will do this thing also that you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken: for you<char style="ord">i</char> have found grace in my sight, and I know you<char style="ord">i</char> by name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, show me you<char style="ord">i</char> glory.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he said, I will make all my goodness pass before you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will proclaim the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> before you<char style="ord">i</char>; and will be gracious to whom I will be gracious, and will show mercy on whom I will show mercy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he said, you<char style="ord">i</char> can not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Behold, <char style="add">[there is]</char> a place by me, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall stand upon a rock:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, while my glory passes by, that I will put you<char style="ord">i</char> in a cleft <char style="pn">(split hoof; an opening, break or split)</char> of the rock, and will cover you<char style="ord">i</char> with my hand while I pass by:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And I will take away my hand, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see my back parts: but my face shall not be seen.</para>
  <chapter number="34" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Hew you<char style="ord">i</char> two tables of stone like unto the first: and I will write upon <char style="add">[these]</char> tables the words that were in the first tables, which you<char style="ord">i</char> broke.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And be ready in the morning, and come up in the morning unto mount Sinai, and present yourself there to me in the top of the mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And no man shall come up with you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither let any man be seen throughout all the mount; neither let the flocks nor herds feed before that mount.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he hewed two tables of stone like unto the first; and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> rose up early in the morning, and went up unto mount Sinai, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded him, and took in his hand the two tables of stone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> descended in the cloud, and stood with him there, and proclaimed the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> passed by before him, and proclaimed, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Keeping mercy for thousands, forgiving iniquity and transgression and sin, and that will by no means clear <char style="add">[the guilty]</char>; visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children, and upon the children’s children, unto the third and to the fourth <char style="add">[generation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> made haste, and bowed his head toward the earth, and worshipped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he said, If now I have found grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> sight, O Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Lord Above All Things]</char>, let my Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Lord Above All Things]</char>, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, go among us; for it <char style="add">[is]</char> a stiff-necked people; and pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us for you<char style="ord">i</char> inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he said, Behold, I make a covenant: before all you<char style="ord">i</char> people I will do marvels, such as have not been done in all the earth, nor in any nation: and all the people among which you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> shall see the work of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for it <char style="add">[is]</char> a terrible thing that I will do with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Observe you<char style="ord">i</char> that which I command you<char style="ord">i</char> this day: behold, I drive out before you<char style="ord">i</char> the Emori <char style="add">[Rebellious Highlanders]</char>, and the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchants]</char>, and the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and the Hivi <char style="add">[Wicked Villagers]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Take heed to yourself, lest you<char style="ord">i</char> make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land to which you<char style="ord">i</char> go, lest it be for a snare in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall destroy their altars, break their images, and cut down their groves:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> shall worship no other god: for the Yehovah Kana <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate is Jealous]</char>, <char style="add">[this is]</char> his very name, El Kana <char style="add">[The Powerful Jealous Living Word]</char> he is:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Lest you<char style="ord">i</char> make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, and they go a whoring after their gods, and do sacrifice unto their gods, and <char style="add">[one]</char> call you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> eat of his sacrifice;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> take of their daughters unto you<char style="ord">i</char> sons, and their daughters go a whoring after their gods, and make you<char style="ord">i</char> sons go a whoring after their gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make you<char style="ord">i</char> no molten gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The feast of unleavened bread shall you<char style="ord">i</char> keep. Seven days you<char style="ord">i</char> shall eat unleavened bread, as I commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>, in the time of the month Aviv: for in the month Aviv you<char style="ord">i</char> came out from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />All that opens the womb <char style="add">[is]</char> my; and every firstling among you<char style="ord">i</char> cattle, <char style="add">[whether]</char> ox or sheep, <char style="add">[that is male]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But the firstling of an ass you<char style="ord">i</char> shall redeem with a lamb: and if you<char style="ord">i</char> redeem <char style="add">[him]</char> not, then shall you<char style="ord">i</char> break his neck. All the firstborn of you<char style="ord">i</char> sons you<char style="ord">i</char> shall redeem. And none shall appear before me empty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Six days you<char style="ord">i</char> shall work, but on the seventh day you<char style="ord">i</char> shall rest: in earing time and in harvest you<char style="ord">i</char> shall rest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall observe the feast of weeks, of the first fruits of wheat harvest, and the feast of ingathering at the year’s end.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Thrice in the year shall all your men children appear before the Lord GOD, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For I will cast out the nations before you<char style="ord">i</char>, and enlarge you<char style="ord">i</char> borders: neither shall any man desire you<char style="ord">i</char> land, when you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go up to appear before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> thrice in the year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leaven; neither shall the sacrifice of the feast of the Passover be left unto the morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />The first of the first fruits of you<char style="ord">i</char> land you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring unto the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not seethe a kid in his mother’s milk.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, Write you<char style="ord">i</char> these words: for after the tenor of these words I have made a covenant with you<char style="ord">i</char> and with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he was there with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water. And he wrote upon the tables the words of the covenant, the ten commandments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> came down from mount Sinai with the two tables of testimony in Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ hand, when he came down from the mount, that Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> did not know not that the skin of his face shone while he talked with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And when Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, behold, the skin of his face shone; and they were afraid to come near him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> called unto them; and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and all the rulers of the congregation returned unto him: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> talked with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And afterward all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came near: and he gave them in commandment all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had spoken with him in mount Sinai.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And <char style="add">[till]</char> Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> had done speaking with them, he put a veil on his face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />But when Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> went in before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to speak with him, he took the veil off, until he came out. And he came out, and spoke unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [that]</char> which he was commanded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw the face of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, that the skin of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>’ face shone: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> put the veil upon his face again, until he went in to speak with him.</para>
  <chapter number="35" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> gathered all the congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> together, and said unto them, These <char style="add">[are]</char> the words which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has commanded, that <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">2f</char>]</char> should do them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Six days shall work be done, but on the seventh day there shall be to you an holy day, a Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> of rest to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: whosoever does work in it shall be put to death.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall kindle no fire throughout your habitations upon the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> spoke unto all the congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Take you<char style="ord">2f</char> from among you an offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: whosoever <char style="add">[is]</char> of a willing heart, let him bring it, an offering of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; gold, and silver, and brass,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And rams’ skins dyed red, and badgers’ skins, and shittim wood,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And oil for the light, and spices for anointing oil, and for the sweet incense,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And onyx stones, and stones to be set for the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and for the breastplate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And every wise hearted among you shall come, and make all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has commanded;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />The tabernacle, his tent, and his covering, his hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char>, and his boards, his bars, his pillars, and his sockets,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The ark, and the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> thereof, <char style="add">[with]</char> the mercy seat, and the veil of the covering,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />The table, and his rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char>, and all his vessels, and the showbread,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The candlestick also for the light, and his furniture, and his lamps, with the oil for the light,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the incense altar, and his rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char>, and the anointing oil, and the sweet incense, and the hanging for the door at the entering in of the tabernacle,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />The altar of burnt offering, with his brazen grate, his rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char>, and all his vessels, the Wash basin and his foot,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />The hangings of the court, his pillars, and their sockets, and the hanging for the door of the court,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The pins of the tabernacle, and the pins of the court, and their cords,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />The cloths of service, to do service in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>, the holy garments for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And all the congregation of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> departed from the presence of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they came, every one whose heart stirred him up, and every one whom his spirit made willing, <char style="add">[and]</char> they brought the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> offering to the work of the tabernacle of the congregation, and for all his service, and for the holy garments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And they came, both men and women, as many as were willing hearted, <char style="add">[and]</char> brought bracelets, and earrings, and rings, and tablets <char style="pn">(small, flat ornaments or jewelry)</char>, all jewels of gold: and every man that offered <char style="add">[offered]</char> an offering of gold unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And every man, with whom was found blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char>, and red skins of rams, and badgers’ skins, brought <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Every one that did offer an offering of silver and brass brought the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> offering: and every man, with whom was found shittim wood for any work of the service, brought <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And all the women that were wise hearted did spin with their hands, and brought that which they had spun, <char style="add">[both]</char> of blue, and of purple, <char style="add">[and]</char> of scarlet, and of fine linen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And all the women whose heart stirred them up in wisdom spun goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the rulers brought onyx stones, and stones to be set, for the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and for the breastplate;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And spice, and oil for the light, and for the anointing oil, and for the sweet incense.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />The people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> brought a willing offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, every man and woman, whose heart made them willing to bring for all manner of work, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded to be made by the hand of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> said unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, See, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has called by name B’tzal’el <char style="add">[In The Shadow (Protection) of El / God]</char> the son of Uri <char style="add">[my light, my fire]</char>, the son of Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char>, of the tribe of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And he has filled him with the spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, in wisdom, in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And to devise detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And in the cutting of stones, to set <char style="add">[them]</char>, and in carving of wood, to make any manner of cunning work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And he has put in his heart that he may teach, <char style="add">[both]</char> he, and Oholi’av <char style="add">[Father’s Tent]</char>, the son of Achisamakh <char style="add">[My Brother is Strength]</char>, of the tribe of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Them has he filled with wisdom of heart, to work all manner of work, of the engraver, and of the cunning workman, and of the embroiderer, in blue, and in purple, in scarlet, and in fine linen, and of the weaver, <char style="add">[even]</char> of them that do any work, and of those that devise cunning work.</para>
  <chapter number="36" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then wrought B’tzal’el <char style="add">[In The Shadow (Protection) of El / God]</char> and Oholi’av <char style="add">[Father’s Tent]</char>, and every wise hearted man, in whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> put wisdom and understanding to know how to work all manner of work for the service of the sanctuary, according to all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> called B’tzal’el <char style="add">[In The Shadow (Protection) of El / God]</char> and Oholi’av <char style="add">[Father’s Tent]</char>, and every wise hearted man, in whose heart the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had put wisdom, <char style="add">[even]</char> every one whose heart stirred him up to come unto the work to do it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they received of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> all the offering, which the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had brought for the work of the service of the sanctuary, to make it <char style="add">[withal]</char>. And they brought yet unto him free offerings every morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And all the wise men, that wrought all the work of the sanctuary, came every man from his work which they made;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying, The people bring much more than enough for the service of the work, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded to make.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> gave commandment, and they caused it to be proclaimed throughout the camp, saying, Let neither man nor woman make any more work for the offering of the sanctuary. So the people were restrained from bringing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For the stuff they had was sufficient for all the work to make it, and too much.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And every wise hearted man among them that wrought the work of the tabernacle made ten curtains <char style="add">[of]</char> fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet: <char style="add">[with]</char> Cherubim of cunning work made he them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The length of one curtain <char style="add">[was]</char> twenty and eight cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: the curtains <char style="add">[were]</char> all of one size.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he coupled the five curtains one unto another: and <char style="add">[the other]</char> five curtains he coupled one unto another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he made loops of blue on the edge of one curtain from the selvedge <char style="pn">(fabric edge to prevent unraveling)</char> in the coupling: likewise he made in the uttermost side of <char style="add">[another]</char> curtain, in the coupling of the second.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Fifty loops made he in one curtain, and fifty loops made he in the edge of the curtain which <char style="add">[was]</char> in the coupling of the second: the loops held one <char style="add">[curtain]</char> to another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he made fifty hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char> of gold, and coupled the curtains one unto another with the hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char>: so it became one tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he made curtains <char style="add">[of]</char> goats’ <char style="add">[hair]</char> for the tent over the tabernacle: eleven curtains he made them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The length of one curtain <char style="add">[was]</char> thirty cubits, and four cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the breadth of one curtain: the eleven curtains <char style="add">[were]</char> of one size.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he coupled five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he made fifty loops upon the uttermost edge of the curtain in the coupling, and fifty loops made he upon the edge of the curtain which couples the second.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he made fifty hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> brass to couple the tent together, that it might be one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he made a covering for the tent <char style="add">[of]</char> rams’ skins dyed red, and a covering <char style="add">[of]</char> badgers’ skins above <char style="add">[that]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he made boards for the tabernacle <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, standing up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />The length of a board <char style="add">[was]</char> ten cubits, and the breadth of a board one cubit and a half.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />One board had two tenons, equally distant one from another: thus did he make for all the boards of the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he made boards for the tabernacle; twenty boards for the south side southward:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And forty sockets of silver he made under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for his two tenons, and two sockets under another board for his two tenons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And for the other side of the tabernacle, <char style="add">[which is]</char> toward the north corner, he made twenty boards,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And their forty sockets of silver; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And for the sides of the tabernacle westward he made six boards.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And two boards made he for the corners of the tabernacle in the two sides.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And they were coupled beneath, and coupled together at the head thereof, to one ring: thus he did to both of them in both the corners.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And there were eight boards; and their sockets <char style="add">[were]</char> sixteen sockets of silver, under every board two sockets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And he made bars of shittim wood; five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the tabernacle for the sides westward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And he made the middle bar to shoot through the boards from the one end to the other.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And he overlaid the boards with gold, and made their rings <char style="add">[of]</char> gold <char style="add">[to be]</char> places for the bars, and overlaid the bars with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And he made a veil <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen: <char style="add">[with]</char> Cherubim made he it of cunning work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And he made thereunto four pillars <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim <char style="add">[wood]</char>, and overlaid them with gold: their hooks <char style="add">[were of]</char> gold; and he cast for them four sockets of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And he made an hanging for the tabernacle door <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, of needlework;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the five pillars of it with their hooks: and he overlaid their columns and their fillets with gold: but their five sockets <char style="add">[were of]</char> brass.</para>
  <chapter number="37" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And B’tzal’el <char style="add">[In The Shadow (Protection) of El / God]</char> made the ark <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood: two cubits and a half <char style="add">[was]</char> the length of it, and a cubit and a half the breadth of it, and a cubit and a half the height of it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he overlaid it with pure gold within and without, and made a crown of gold to it round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he cast for it four rings of gold, <char style="add">[to be set]</char> by the four corners of it; even two rings upon the one side of it, and two rings upon the other side of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he made rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlaid them with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he put the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> into the rings by the sides of the ark, to bear the ark.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he made the mercy seat <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold: two cubits and a half <char style="add">[was]</char> the length thereof, and one cubit and a half the breadth thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he made two Cherubim <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, beaten out of one piece made he them, on the two ends of the mercy seat;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />One cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> on the end on this side, and another cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> on the <char style="add">[other]</char> end on that side: out of the mercy seat made he the Cherubim on the two ends thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the Cherubim spread out <char style="add">[their]</char> wings on high, <char style="add">[and]</char> covered with their wings over the mercy seat, with their faces one to another; <char style="add">[even]</char> to the mercy seatward were the faces of the Cherubim.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he made the table <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood: two cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he overlaid it with pure gold, and made thereunto a crown of gold round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Also he made thereunto a border of an handbreadth round about; and made a crown of gold for the border thereof round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he cast for it four rings of gold, and put the rings upon the four corners that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the four feet thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Over against the border were the rings, the places for the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> to bear the table.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he made the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlaid them with gold, to bear the table.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he made the vessels which <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the table, his dishes, and his spoons, and his bowls, and his covers to cover withal, <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he made the candlestick <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold: <char style="add">[of]</char> beaten work made he the candlestick; his shaft, and his branch, his bowls, his knops, and his flowers, were of the same:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And six branches going out of the sides thereof; three branches of the candlestick out of the one side thereof, and three branches of the candlestick out of the other side thereof:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Three bowls made after the fashion of almonds in one branch, a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> and a flower; and three bowls made like almonds in another branch, a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> and a flower: so throughout the six branches going out of the candlestick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And in the candlestick <char style="add">[were]</char> four bowls made like almonds, his knops, and his flowers:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> under two branches of the same, and a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> under two branches of the same, and a knob <char style="pn">(flower bud)</char> under two branches of the same, according to the six branches going out of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Their knops and their branches were of the same: all of it <char style="add">[was]</char> one beaten work <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he made his seven lamps, and his snuffers, and his snuff dishes, <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Of]</char> a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> of pure gold made he it, and all the vessels thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And he made the incense altar <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood: the length of it <char style="add">[was]</char> a cubit, and the breadth of it a cubit; <char style="add">[it was]</char> Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char>; and two cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the height of it; the horns thereof were of the same.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he overlaid it with pure gold, <char style="add">[both]</char> the top of it, and the sides thereof round about, and the horns of it: also he made unto it a crown of gold round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he made two rings of gold for it under the crown thereof, by the two corners of it, upon the two sides thereof, to be places for the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> to bear it withal.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he made the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlaid them with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And he made the holy anointing oil, and the pure incense of sweet spices, according to the work of the apothecary.</para>
  <chapter number="38" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And he made the altar of burnt offering <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood: five cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the length thereof, and five cubits the breadth thereof; <char style="add">[it was]</char> Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char>; and three cubits the height thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he made the horns thereof on the four corners of it; the horns thereof were of the same: and he overlaid it with brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he made all the vessels of the altar, the pots, and the shovels, and the basins, <char style="add">[and]</char> the flesh hooks, and the firepans: all the vessels thereof made he <char style="add">[of]</char> brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he made for the altar a brazen grate of network under the compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> thereof beneath unto the midst of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he cast four rings for the four ends of the grate of brass, <char style="add">[to be]</char> places for the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he made the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> shittim wood, and overlaid them with brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he put the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> into the rings on the sides of the altar, to bear it withal; he made the altar hollow with boards.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he made the Wash basin <char style="add">[of]</char> brass, and the foot of it <char style="add">[of]</char> brass, of the looking glasses of <char style="add">[the women]</char> assembling, which assembled <char style="add">[at]</char> the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he made the court: on the south side southward the hangings of the court <char style="add">[were of]</char> fine twined linen, an hundred cubits:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Their pillars <char style="add">[were]</char> twenty, and their brazen sockets twenty; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets <char style="add">[were of]</char> silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And for the north side <char style="add">[the hangings were]</char> an hundred cubits, their pillars <char style="add">[were]</char> twenty, and their sockets of brass twenty; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets <char style="add">[of]</char> silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And for the west side <char style="add">[were]</char> hangings of fifty cubits, their pillars ten, and their sockets ten; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets <char style="add">[of]</char> silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And for the east side eastward fifty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The hangings of the one side <char style="add">[of the gate were]</char> fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And for the other side of the court gate, on this hand and that hand, <char style="add">[were]</char> hangings of fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />All the hangings of the court round about <char style="add">[were]</char> of fine twined linen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the sockets for the pillars <char style="add">[were of]</char> brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets <char style="add">[of]</char> silver; and the overlaying of their columns <char style="add">[of]</char> silver; and all the pillars of the court <char style="add">[were]</char> filleted with silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the hanging for the gate of the court <char style="add">[was]</char> needlework, <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen: and twenty cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the length, and the height in the breadth <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits, answerable to the hangings of the court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And their pillars <char style="add">[were]</char> four, and their sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> brass four; their hooks <char style="add">[of]</char> silver, and the overlaying of their columns and their fillets <char style="add">[of]</char> silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And all the pins of the tabernacle, and of the court round about, <char style="add">[were of]</char> brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />This is the sum of the tabernacle, <char style="add">[even]</char> of the tabernacle of testimony, as it was counted, according to the commandment of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, <char style="add">[for]</char> the service of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, by the hand of Itamar <char style="add">[Coast of Palms]</char>, son to Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the priest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And B’tzal’el <char style="add">[In The Shadow (Protection) of El / God]</char> the son of Uri <char style="add">[my light, my fire]</char>, the son of Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char>, of the tribe of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, made all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And with him <char style="add">[was]</char> Oholi’av <char style="add">[Father’s Tent]</char>, son of Achisamakh <char style="add">[My Brother is Strength]</char>, of the tribe of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, an engraver, and a cunning workman, and an embroiderer in blue, and in purple, and in scarlet, and fine linen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />All the gold that was occupied for the work in all the work of the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>, even the gold of the offering, was twenty and nine talents, and seven hundred and thirty shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the silver of them that were numbered of the congregation <char style="add">[was]</char> an hundred talents, and a thousand seven hundred and threescore and fifteen shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />A bekah for every man, <char style="add">[that is]</char>, half a shekel, after the shekel of the sanctuary, for every one that went to be numbered, from twenty years old and upward, for six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty <char style="add">[men]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And of the hundred talents of silver were cast the sockets of the sanctuary, and the sockets of the veil; an hundred sockets of the hundred talents, a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> for a socket.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And of the thousand seven hundred seventy and five shekels he made hooks for the pillars, and overlaid their columns, and filleted them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the brass of the offering <char style="add">[was]</char> seventy talents, and two thousand and four hundred shekels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And with that he made the sockets to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and the brazen altar, and the brazen grate for it, and all the vessels of the altar,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the sockets of the court round about, and the sockets of the court gate, and all the pins of the tabernacle, and all the pins of the court round about.</para>
  <chapter number="39" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And of the blue, and purple, and scarlet, they made cloths of service, to do service in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>, and made the holy garments for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he made the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they did beat the gold into thin plates, and cut <char style="add">[it into]</char> wires, to work <char style="add">[it]</char> in the blue, and in the purple, and in the scarlet, and in the fine linen, <char style="add">[with]</char> cunning work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />They made shoulder pieces for it, to couple <char style="add">[it]</char> together: by the two edges was it coupled together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> belt of his ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, that <char style="add">[was]</char> upon it, <char style="add">[was]</char> of the same, according to the work thereof; <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they wrought onyx stones enclosed in sockets of gold, graven, as signets are graven, with the names of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he put them on the shoulders of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, <char style="add">[that they should be]</char> stones for a memorial to the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he made the breastplate <char style="add">[of]</char> cunning work, like the work of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>; <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />It was Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char>; they made the breastplate double: a span <char style="add">[was]</char> the length thereof, and a span the breadth thereof, <char style="add">[being]</char> doubled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they set in it four rows of stones: <char style="add">[the first]</char> row <char style="add">[was]</char> a sardius, a topaz, and a Carbuncle <char style="pn">(a red precious stone)</char>: this <char style="add">[was]</char> the first row.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the second row, an emerald, a sapphire, and a diamond.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the third row, a ligure, an agate, and an amethyst.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the fourth row, a beryl, an onyx, and a jasper: <char style="add">[they were]</char> enclosed in sockets of gold in their inclosings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the stones <char style="add">[were]</char> according to the names of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, twelve, according to their names, <char style="add">[like]</char> the engravings of a signet <char style="pn">(seal or stamp)</char>, everyone with his name, according to the twelve tribes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they made upon the breastplate chains at the ends, <char style="add">[of]</char> wreathen work <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they made two sockets <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, and two gold rings; and put the two rings in the two ends of the breastplate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they put the two wreathen chains of gold in the two rings on the ends of the breastplate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the two ends of the two wreathen chains they fastened in the two sockets, and put them on the shoulder pieces of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, before it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they made two rings of gold, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> on the two ends of the breastplate, upon the border of it, which <char style="add">[was]</char> on the side of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> inward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And they made two <char style="add">[other]</char> golden rings, and put them on the two sides of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> underneath, toward the forepart of it, over against the <char style="add">[other]</char> coupling thereof, above the detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> belt of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they did bind the breastplate by his rings unto the rings of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> with a lace of blue, that it might be above the detailed <char style="pn">(skillfully made)</char> belt of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>, and that the breastplate might not be loosed from the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And he made the robe of the ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> woven work, all <char style="add">[of]</char> blue.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there was]</char> an hole in the midst of the robe, as the hole of an habergeon <char style="pn">(coat of mail for the neck and down)</char>, <char style="add">[with]</char> a band round about the hole, that it should not rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And they made upon the hems of the robe pomegranates <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and scarlet, <char style="add">[and]</char> twined <char style="add">[linen]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they made bells <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold, and put the bells between the pomegranates upon the hem of the robe, round about between the pomegranates;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />A bell and a pomegranate, a bell and a pomegranate, round about the hem of the robe to minister <char style="add">[in]</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And they made coats <char style="add">[of]</char> fine linen <char style="add">[of]</char> woven work for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and for his sons,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And a mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> fine linen, and goodly bonnets <char style="add">[of]</char> fine linen, and linen trousers <char style="add">[of]</char> fine twined linen,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And a belt <char style="add">[of]</char> fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet, <char style="add">[of]</char> needlework; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And they made the plate of the holy crown <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold, and wrote upon it a writing, <char style="add">[like to]</char> the engravings of a signet <char style="pn">(seal or stamp)</char>, HOLINESS TO THE LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And they tied unto it a lace of blue, to fasten <char style="add">[it]</char> on high upon the mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Thus was all the work of the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation finished: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did according to all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, so did they.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And they brought the tabernacle unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, the tent, and all his furniture, his hooks <char style="pn">(fasteners)</char>, his boards, his bars, and his pillars, and his sockets,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the covering of rams’ skins dyed red, and the covering of badgers’ skins, and the veil of the covering,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />The ark of the testimony, and the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> thereof, and the mercy seat,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />The table, <char style="add">[and]</char> all the vessels thereof, and the showbread,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />The pure candlestick, <char style="add">[with]</char> the lamps thereof, <char style="add">[even with]</char> the lamps to be set in order, and all the vessels thereof, and the oil for light,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the golden altar, and the anointing oil, and the sweet incense, and the hanging for the tabernacle door,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />The brazen altar, and his grate of brass, his rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char>, and all his vessels, the Wash basin and his foot,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />The hangings of the court, his pillars, and his sockets, and the hanging for the court gate, his cords, and his pins, and all the vessels of the service of the tabernacle, for the tent of the congregation,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />The cloths of service to do service in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>, and the holy garments for Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the priest, and his sons’ garments, to minister in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />According to all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, so the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> made all the work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> did look upon all the work, and, behold, they had done it as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded, even so had they done it: and Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> them.</para>
  <chapter number="40" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />On the first day of the first month shall you<char style="ord">i</char> set up the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put in it the ark of the testimony, and cover the ark with the veil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring in the table, and set in order the things that are to be set in order upon it; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring in the candlestick, and light the lamps thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set the altar of gold for the incense before the ark of the testimony, and put the hanging of the door to the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set the altar of the burnt offering before the door of the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set the Wash basin between the tent of the congregation and the altar, and shall put water in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set up the court round about, and hang up the hanging at the court gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take the anointing oil, and anoint the tabernacle, and all that <char style="add">[is]</char> in it, and shall hallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> it, and all the vessels thereof: and it shall be holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint the altar of the burnt offering, and all his vessels, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> the altar: and it shall be an altar most holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint the Wash basin and his foot, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and wash them with water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall put upon Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the holy garments, and anoint him, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> him; that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring his sons, and clothe them with coats:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall anoint them, as you<char style="ord">i</char> did anoint their father, that they may minister unto me in the priest’s office: for their anointing shall surely be an everlasting priesthood throughout their generations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Thus did Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>: according to all that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded him, so did he.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it came to pass in the first month in the second year, on the first <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> the tabernacle was reared up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> reared up the tabernacle, and fastened his sockets, and set up the boards thereof, and put in the bars thereof, and reared up his pillars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he spread abroad the tent over the tabernacle, and put the covering of the tent above upon it; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he took and put the testimony into the ark, and set the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> on the ark, and put the mercy seat above upon the ark:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he brought the ark into the tabernacle, and set up the veil of the covering, and covered the ark of the testimony; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And he put the table in the tent of the congregation, upon the side of the tabernacle northward, without the veil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he set the bread in order upon it before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he put the candlestick in the tent of the congregation, over against the table, on the side of the tabernacle southward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And he lighted the lamps before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he put the golden altar in the tent of the congregation before the veil:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he burnt sweet incense thereon; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he set up the hanging <char style="add">[at]</char> the door of the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And he put the altar of burnt offering <char style="add">[by]</char> the door of the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation, and offered upon it the burnt offering and the meat offering; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And he set the Wash basin between the tent of the congregation and the altar, and put water there, to wash <char style="add">[withal]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> and Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> and his sons washed their hands and their feet thereat:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />When they went into the tent of the congregation, and when they came near unto the altar, they washed; as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And he reared up the court round about the tabernacle and the altar, and set up the hanging of the court gate. So Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> finished the work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Then a cloud covered the tent of the congregation, and the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> filled the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> was not able to enter into the tent of the congregation, because the cloud abode thereon, and the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> filled the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And when the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle, the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went onward in all their journeys:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />But if the cloud were not taken up, then they journeyed not till the day that it was taken up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />For the cloud of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> upon the tabernacle by day, and fire was on it by night, in the sight of all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, throughout all their journeys.</para>
</usx>